window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["1f"]={"https://theconversation.com/new-ai-regulator-announced-as-government-considers-criminal-law-change-to-keep-erring-frontier-companies-in-line-296274":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"788e55d5cf00c5ab2228b6a5dc01886223d3563aefda45f7445b32feca7182c3","read":"https://theconversation.com/new-ai-regulator-announced-as-government-considers-criminal-law-change-to-keep-erring-frontier-companies-in-line-296274","bytes":175073,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"New AI regulator announced, as government considers criminal law change to keep erring frontier companies in line","by":[{"n":"Michelle Grattan","r":"Professorial Fellow, University of Canberra"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T04:58:32Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Prime Minister Anthony Albanese has announced a new artificial intelligence (AI) safety regulator, which will enforce penalties for frontier AI companies that breach their obligations."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government is also considering criminal law changes to deal with serious misconduct by any of these companies."]},{"k":"p","s":["The measures are targeted at frontier AI companies – those building the largest, most advanced models."]},{"k":"p","s":["At a news conference shortly before leaving for the COP climate conference in Turkey, the prime minister outlined AI safety and security protections that will be in the government’s proposed AI framework legislation."]},{"k":"p","s":["The six mandated requirements for companies are:"]},{"k":"li","s":["maintain security controls across all stages of AI development and deployment"]},{"k":"li","s":["identify and manage serious risks associated with models"]},{"k":"li","s":["quickly provide mandatory notification of incidents to the Australian government"]},{"k":"li","s":["allow independent evaluation of models"]},{"k":"li","s":["maintain and publish safety and security frameworks to ensure good governance, risk management and transparency"]},{"k":"li","s":["respond to updated standards and rules as technologies change."]},{"k":"p","s":["Albanese said these protections were in line with recommendations from the parliamentary joint select committee on AI."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government also released the recommendations from the rapid review into the OpenAI breach of an Australian government site by a rogue agent earlier this year."]},{"k":"p","s":["In this breach, for which OpenAI apologised, statistical health data was accessed, but no personal data. The government complained strongly to the company."]},{"k":"p","s":["“It can’t be allowed to happen again,” Albanese said on Tuesday. He said the government had accepted and commenced work on the review’s 18 recommendations."]},{"k":"p","s":["The recommendations include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["mandatory AI company reporting of misaligned behaviour or cyber incidents"]},{"k":"li","s":["consideration of reforming criminal law to deal with cases of serious misconduct"]},{"k":"li","s":["greater engagement with international counterparts and frontier AI developers to promote shared expectations about AI safety and accountability"]},{"k":"li","s":["strengthening resilience and response to AI incidents, including better information sharing and more focus on cyber security."]},{"k":"p","s":["Albanese, appearing with Defence Minister Richard Marles and Home Affairs Minister Tony Burke, told his news conference the government wanted to see Australia benefiting from the advantages of AI while mitigating the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["In relation to new criminal penalties the review report said the Attorney-General’s Department, in consultation with the Australian Federal Police, the Home Affair Department, and other agencies, should explore:"]},{"k":"p","s":["the application of criminal penalties for egregious regulatory non-compliance; and/or a standalone “failure to prevent” offence which would criminalise instances where the company is responsible for developing an AI model that engages in harmful conduct, and the company fails to take reasonable steps to prevent that harm."]},{"k":"p","s":["Albanese said the government would release the report of the review, with due regard to national security considerations, but there is no clarity about when this will be done."]}],"chars":3059},"https://theconversation.com/was-a-kinder-fate-possible-for-marinelands-animals-how-the-planning-process-failed-them-295643":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"aa86a5b0338064143cf755e30de0843f883b2031538d1accb4b8ae9e391c354f","read":"https://theconversation.com/was-a-kinder-fate-possible-for-marinelands-animals-how-the-planning-process-failed-them-295643","bytes":184029,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Was a kinder fate possible for Marineland’s animals? How the planning process failed them","by":[{"n":"Pooja Kumar","r":"PhD Student, School of Planning, University of Waterloo"}],"pub":"2026-11-15T15:20:51Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Peekachu, Rain, Osiris, Caspian, Jellybean and Cyprus ",["are dead","https://www.independent.co.uk/news/world/americas/canada-beluga-whale-shedd-aquarium-b3078474.html"],". They were six of the 30 beluga whales removed from Marineland in Niagara Falls earlier this year. Echo is dead too. She was one of the four dolphins who were also removed around the same time. For all intents and purposes, ",["she was blind","https://animaljustice.ca/blog/beluga-dies-after-marineland-export-as-2-belugas-4-dolphins-are-shipped-to-spain"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["I think about the ",["rocks and paint that have been found in the belugas’ stomachs","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/marineland-beluga-deaths-preliminary-necropsy-findings-chicago-9.7358828"]," through autopsies. I dwell on how a place designed to hold them captive was legitimized for years. Jellybean was born at Marineland 19 years ago and gave birth there, too."]},{"k":"p","s":[["My profession — planning","https://www.cip-icu.ca/about-us/planning/"]," — had a role to play in facilitating their deaths and in allowing suffering during their lives. Planning has many specializations: urban, rural, regional, housing and transportation are a few."]},{"k":"p","s":["I am a Registered Professional Planner who specialized in environmental planning during graduate school. My work over the past 20 years, though, has often been more about what land can be used for and how it’s used."]},{"k":"p","s":["Marineland has been around since the 1960s. ",["Its record of bad things happening to animals only grew over time","https://thewalrus.ca/the-marineland-dreamland/"],". I can now see how the mistreatment of the whales and dolphins was inevitable."]},{"k":"h","s":["The orientation of planning"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Planning has been a formal occupation in Canada since 1919","https://www.cip-icu.ca/our-history/"],". It has the legal status of a self-regulating profession now. Planners often work for governments, especially municipalities. Personally, I’ve analyzed land-use plans as a consultant."]},{"k":"p","s":["In my work for a provincial government, I’ve told other planners what needs to change before a plan or its implementing bylaw can be approved. And as a municipal planner, I’ve made decisions about how humans can use land."]},{"k":"p","s":["The City of Niagara Falls’ Official Plan describes Marineland as ",["“family entertainment.”","https://media-002-ca.cdn.govstack.com/niagarafallsbusiness-009-ca/media/hdbpag0k/official-plan-2024-january-9-consolidation-accessible.pdf"]," No words in this legal planning document speak to the conditions the sea mammals needed to survive, let alone thrive. Yet it’s the document that legitimized Marineland’s existence."]},{"k":"h","s":["The nails in the coffins"]},{"k":"p","s":["A ",["February 2025 Committee of Adjustment meeting","https://niagarafalls.civicweb.net/document/91289/?printPdf=true"]," haunts me. Committees of Adjustment are a sub-structure of municipal governments in Ontario. They are allowed under Section 44 of the provincial government’s ",["Planning Act","https://www.ontario.ca/laws/statute/90p13#BK72"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Committees of Adjustment make decisions about proposed changes to land that are minor, and that also don’t meet the requirements in municipal planning documents. Since these committees are a planning mechanism, planning staff help them do their work."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Niagara Falls committee considered eight different applications about Marineland in February 2025. ",["Each was approved","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/hamilton/marineland-property-severance-1.7463678"],". Together, they brought Marineland into compliance with the city’s Official Plan and Zoning Bylaw. Niagara Falls adopted a new ",["Official Plan","https://niagarafalls.ca/building-planning-and-business/planning-and-development/long-range-plans-and-studies/official-plan/"]," in August 2026, which is still awaiting approval from the provincial government."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many wheels need to be set in motion before an actual application to eventually redevelop land materializes. This was one of those wheels."]},{"k":"p","s":["After the February 2025 meeting, Marineland applied for ",["federal approval","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/hamilton/marineland-export-permission-belugas-1.7640593"]," to export the whales and dolphins (which was at first denied), then said that it would ",["euthanize them","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/hamilton/marineland-belugas-dolphins-9.7057017"]," (more than once) and finally received ",["federal approval","https://www.thecanadianpressnews.ca/ontario/ottawa-gives-conditional-approval-for-marineland-to-export-remaining-belugas-to-u-s/article_1bd33332-6f1d-5907-a117-86584bd85859.html"]," to export them."]},{"k":"h","s":["Hierarchies of power and public processes"]},{"k":"p","s":["The planning process can be the only public opportunity to point out something that could, otherwise, go unnoticed. At the February 2025 meeting, people expressed concerns about what would happen to Marineland’s whales and dolphins."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some attendees asked the committee to defer its decision until there was more information about how the animals on the site would be treated. Marineland’s representative suggested that the approvals they sought were unrelated ",["to animal welfare","https://thestarfish.ca/journal/2026/04/behind-the-show-curtains-marinelands-deceitful-history-and-the-search-for-justice"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Marineland had asked for variances, easements, new parcel creation and mortgage release to secure operational financing. The municipality’s planners had evaluated the applications as minor, based on how there was no actual development being proposed, how no neighbouring properties would be impacted and how streetscape and character wouldn’t be compromised."]},{"k":"p","s":["If it sounds like jargon, that’s because it is. Over time, planning has become a profession with its own language and processes. Often, when I’m talking to a non-planner, I’m simply translating."]},{"k":"p","s":["The planning priorities in the jargon are not unusual either. Mechanisms like Committees of Adjustment have also been called out for ",["reducing greater public participation","https://digitalcommons.pepperdine.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=2635&context=plr"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Finding a better way"]},{"k":"p","s":["Peekachu, Rain, Osiris, Caspian, Jellybean, Cyprus and Echo didn’t fit into the planning process. Sweden-based planning theorist Jonathan Metzger calls the effect ",["“radical exclusion.”","https://doi.org/10.1080/13604813.2016.1193997"]]},{"k":"p","s":["As a practitioner who has turned to a PhD, I’m painfully aware that planners think not in terms of life, but land. The Canadian planning profession’s most recent update to its ",["ethical standards","https://psb-planningcanada.ca/standards/"]," doesn’t do animals justice either."]},{"k":"p","s":["Marineland’s tanks and enclosures may be empty now. Fur farms, factory farms, testing labs and zoos still stand. The path to different futures is not easy. Animals are legally property. So is land. There is urgency, though, and a need for answers that are kinder than the status quo."]},{"k":"p","s":[["In their new book","https://doi.org/10.1057/s41296-026-00833-9"],", Animals and The Right to Politics, philosophy scholars Sue Donaldson and Will Kymlicka imagine a city with two distinct governance systems. In addition to the existing municipal government, they propose a new political entity that takes over land and development decisions. The intention is to create a more stable, peaceful world for animals."]},{"k":"p","s":["Plausible or not, we must move towards some new normal. Humanity is a hollow word if we don’t. But I don’t see it happening unless non-planners insist that planning work consider every sentient being, not just humans."]}],"chars":5682},"https://theconversation.com/who-does-budget-2026-help-not-the-1-in-3-canadians-skipping-meals-to-cope-with-grocery-costs-294442":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"a6e0c9f6b810170be03ecca4d1d7eb4b65877fd6231f305052cb59f5ed56f778","read":"https://theconversation.com/who-does-budget-2026-help-not-the-1-in-3-canadians-skipping-meals-to-cope-with-grocery-costs-294442","bytes":188417,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Who does Budget 2026 help? Not the 1 in 3 Canadians skipping meals to cope with grocery costs","by":[{"n":"Tracy Smith-Carrier","r":"Professor and Canada Research Chair (Tier 2) in Advancing the UN Sustainable Development Goals, Royal Roads University"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T15:59:08Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["In his 2021 book Value(s): Building a Better World for All, Mark Carney, now prime minister, wrote: ",["“Companies exist to improve our lives, expand our horizons and solve society’s problems.”","https://www.penguinrandomhouse.ca/books/669023/values-by-mark-carney/9780771051579"]]},{"k":"p","s":["His government’s ",["Budget 2026","https://budget.canada.ca/2026/home-accueil-en.html"],", tabled Nov. 5 under the title “Masters of Our Destiny,” puts that belief into practice. It spends far more public funds rewarding and “incentivizing” the owners of large companies than it does addressing the affordability challenges Canadians face."]},{"k":"p","s":["The budget offers tax breaks on ",["private investment and capital gains, along with write-offs on capital purchases such as equipment. Corporations will collect them on investments they likely would have made anyway","https://www.policyalternatives.ca/news-research/budget-2026-canada-goes-all-in-on-corporate-profits/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is trickle-down economics, ",["and it doesn’t work","https://www.weforum.org/stories/financial-and-monetary-systems/tax-cuts-for-wealthy-impact-lse-study"],". Corporate welfare sends profits gushing up to the wealthy ",["without necessarily yielding spillovers","https://budget.canada.ca/2026/report-rapport/pdf/budget-2026.pdf"]," in ",["jobs or economic growth.","https://www.lse.ac.uk/research/research-for-the-world/economics/tax-cuts-for-the-wealthy-only-benefit-the-rich-debunking-trickle-down-economics"]]},{"k":"h","s":["More Canadians are going without"]},{"k":"p","s":["A string of reports released in recent weeks ",["underscores the urgency of the moment","https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/programs/poverty-reduction/national-advisory-council/reports/2026-annual.html"],". Apart from much-needed funding for housing and a welcome commitment to end homelessness within 10 years, the budget talks more about income and food security than it actually delivers."]},{"k":"p","s":[["The National Advisory Council on Poverty’s 2026 report, Too Many Left Behind,","https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/programs/poverty-reduction/national-advisory-council/reports/2026-annual.html"]," finds Canada is not on track to meet its commitment to cut poverty in half by 2030."]},{"k":"p","s":["While poverty fell between 2015 and 2020, ",["it has climbed steadily since 2021","https://www.canada.ca/content/dam/esdc-edsc/documents/programs/poverty-reduction/national-advisory-council/reports/2025-annual/NACP_2025_Annual_Report-EN.pdf"],". Food Banks Canada’s 2026 HungerCount report indicates that food bank visits have ",["risen 117 per cent since 2019, and are almost nine per cent higher than last year","https://foodbankscanada.ca/hunger-in-canada/hungercount/"],". Toronto’s Daily Bread Food Bank documents a whopping ",["333 per cent increase over the same period","https://www.dailybread.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/DB-WHR-Report-2026-Digital.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Salvation Army’s national report found that 31 per cent of Canadians surveyed in September had ",["skipped meals or reduced their portion size because they couldn’t afford groceries","https://salvationarmy.ca/salvation-army-report-finds-nearly-one-in-three-canadians-skipping-meals-as-food-insecurity-hits-four-year-high/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Employment alone doesn’t guarantee food security either. The main earners in two-thirds of food-insecure households ",["hold permanent, full-time jobs","https://thetyee.ca/News/2026/02/06/Even-Full-Time-Workers-Struggle-Afford-Food/"],". Financial strain doesn’t just affect people with low incomes, ",["although they feel it most acutely","https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/programs/poverty-reduction/backgrounder.html#h2.4"]," — the ",["middle class is also feeling the squeeze","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/middle-class-voters-1.7494434"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada’s official poverty line misses much of this. The material deprivation index captures the number of households that ",["can’t afford items or activities that most would identify as essential for a decent living standard","https://foodbankscanada.ca/5-things-you-should-know-about-using-a-material-deprivation-index-to-measure-poverty/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Using 2023 data, Geranda Notten, a University of Ottawa professor of public policy, and colleagues found one in four Canadian adults couldn’t ",["“afford two or more items that most people view as necessary to achieve an acceptable standard of living in Canada.”","https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Michael-Mendelson/publication/381506545_Material_deprivation_-_An_updated_index_for_Canada/links/66831a42f3b61c4e2ca27a85/Material-deprivation-An-updated-index-for-Canada.pdf"]]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2026, Richard Matern, director of research at Food Banks Canada, and colleagues found ",["28 per cent of people in Canada were living at a poverty-level standard","https://policyoptions.irpp.org/2026/08/poverty-measures-canada/"],". That is a far starker picture than the ",["11 per cent estimated by the Market Basket Measure","https://www.canada.ca/content/dam/esdc-edsc/documents/programs/poverty-reduction/national-advisory-council/reports/2026-annual/NACP_2026_Annual_Report-en.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["The case for a basic income"]},{"k":"p","s":["Charity ",["isn’t effective in remedying poverty and hunger","https://doi.org/10.1007/s41134-020-00124-2"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Food banks can’t lift people out of poverty","https://policyoptions.irpp.org/2018/09/rights-based-approach-key-alleviating-poverty/"],", and ",["because food security depends on income","https://doi.org/10.3138/CPP.38.4.4"],", ",["you can’t address hunger unless you improve people’s financial status","https://canadianfoodstudies.uwaterloo.ca/index.php/cfs/article/view/748"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["We spend huge amounts ",["treating poverty’s symptoms","https://www.canada.ca/en/employment-social-development/programs/poverty-reduction/national-advisory-council/reports/2025-annual.html"],", and we do it ineffectively. That’s where a ",["basic income guarantee","https://www.ubiworks.ca/blog/consensus-statement"]," becomes attractive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["A guaranteed basic income could end poverty, so why isn’t it happening?","https://theconversation.com/a-guaranteed-basic-income-could-end-poverty-so-why-isnt-it-happening-182638"]]},{"k":"p","s":[["Its principles include","https://canadianfoodstudies.uwaterloo.ca/index.php/cfs/article/view/748"]," adequacy (incomes above poverty thresholds), non-conditionality (no strings attached), dignity (little stigma) and universal access (support for everyone who needs it). It rests on ",["feminist principles of economic justice and human rights","https://actbig.ca/guiding-principles/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["A wealth of evidence shows that cash transfer experiments and basic income pilots have positive outcomes: ",["better food and nutrition","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1111/1467-9566.70261"],", ",["improved housing stability","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/abs/10.1080/10875549.2019.1616242"],", ",["lower hospitalization rates","https://utppublishing.com/doi/abs/10.3138/cpp.37.3.283"],", ",["reduced gender-based violence","https://www.degruyterbrill.com/document/doi/10.1515/bis-2022-0032/html"],", ",["enhanced educational performance","https://books.google.ca/books?hl=en&lr=&id=HQ9xDwAAQBAJ&oi=fnd&pg=PA7&dq=basic+income+canada+improves+educational+performance&ots=MyJ93cUK7g&sig=jlxotX3g9_hgWksoJY5Lpz_DQns#v=onepage&q&f=false"],", ",["less worry and stress.","https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1155/hsc/7816069"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Patching an inadequate system"]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada’s income security programs are too small to change people’s finances in meaningful ways. Their narrow eligibility rules leave many people falling through the cracks, particularly ",["working-age adults","https://maytree.com/publications/stubbornly-high-canadas-poverty-reduction-efforts-have-stalled/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["These programs aren’t built to tackle poverty or the affordability crisis, and the new budget does little to change that."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take the ",["Canada Child Benefit","https://www.canada.ca/en/revenue-agency/services/child-family-benefits/canada-child-benefit.html"],", a proven ",["poverty-reduction tool","https://www.journals.uchicago.edu/doi/abs/10.1086/721379"],". Many credit its overhaul with the ",["significant drop in poverty in the late 2010s","https://temertymedicine.utoronto.ca/news/canada-child-benefit-has-led-major-reduction-severe-food-insecurity-study-suggests"],". But ",["child poverty is on the rise again as living costs outpace benefits","https://campaign2000.ca/new-release-2025-report-card-on-child-and-family-poverty-in-canada/"],", and Budget 2026 doesn’t commit to increasing the benefit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nor does the budget improve the ",["Canada Disability Benefit","https://www.canada.ca/en/services/benefits/disability/canada-disability-benefit.html"],", which pays at most ",["about $200 a month and comes with eligibility barriers","https://cjds.uwaterloo.ca/index.php/cjds/article/view/1298"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["No new spending was earmarked for the Canada Social Transfer, which funds provincial and territorial social programs and services, including social assistance programs. These programs are mired in ",["stigma","https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s41134-020-00124-2"]," and ",["dehumanizing indignities","https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/social-policy-and-society/article/i-was-trusted-for-once-imagining-more-humane-income-supports-through-the-ontario-basic-income-pilot/C92C2564BF8BF871A8BBF337CB574AA4"],". Rather than alleviating financial deprivation, ",["they trap people in deep poverty","https://irpp.org/research-studies/canadas-forgotten-poor-putting-singles-living-in-deep-poverty-on-the-policy-radar/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["What Budget 2026 did fund was another ",["one-time top-up","https://budget.canada.ca/2026/report-rapport/chap3-en.html"]," to the ",["Canada Groceries and Essentials Benefit","https://www.canada.ca/en/revenue-agency/services/child-family-benefits/canada-groceries-essentials-benefit.html"],": up to $339 for a single person without children and up to $679 for a couple with two children. That’s likely enough to cover ",["about two grocery bills","https://www.grocerysaver.ca/blog/how-much-canadians-spend-on-groceries-per-month-2026/"],". To make a real dent, the benefit ",["needs a lasting boost.","https://maytree.com/publications/a-step-in-the-right-direction-the-new-canada-groceries-and-essentials-benefit-in-context/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["The budget also proposes making the ",["Canada Caregiver Credit","https://budget.canada.ca/2026/report-rapport/chap3-en.html"]," refundable, worth up to $1,260 a year. It would rename the Canada Workers Benefit the ",["Build Canada Workers Benefit","https://budget.canada.ca/2026/report-rapport/chap3-en.html"],", slightly widening eligibility and raising the maximum for single people to $1,859 a year from $1,709."]},{"k":"p","s":["These are helpful steps, but they aren’t robust enough while costs keep soaring."]},{"k":"h","s":["Who the budget really serves"]},{"k":"p","s":["At a time when Canada should be ",["introducing wealth taxes","https://www.dundurn.com/books_/t22117/a9781459754836-cancelling-billionaires-before-they-cancel-us"]," to curb ",["dangerous levels of inequality","https://www.oxfam.ca/story/inequality-kills/"],", the budget’s centrepiece is the Productivity Mega Deduction. Estimated to cost $36 billion over five years, it offers corporations new cash and tax incentives."]},{"k":"p","s":["A basic income, by contrast, is cost-effective and ",["has majority public support","https://angusreid.org/universal-basic-income-covid19/"],". It would help not only the people who receive it, but also ",["everyone who worries they might one day need it","https://doi.org/10.1155/hsc/7816069"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Canadians need long-term investments in their health and security. One-time top-ups and tinkering with existing, largely inadequate programs won’t cut it. Budget 2026 delivers a huge cash transfer to shareholders and the C-suite."]},{"k":"p","s":["So whose futures were the ",["“masters of our destiny”","https://budget.canada.ca/2026/report-rapport/pdf/budget-2026.pdf"]," thinking about when they wrote this budget?"]}],"chars":6397},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/south-korea":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"a08186ff6c0f32bc159f2a54f1fd3cc4576c13031c8aa1a842897b39a84c4343","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/south-korea","bytes":76497,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"South Korea travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-12T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-05-14T11:06:39+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Global travel impacts due to escalation in the Middle East"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escalation in the Middle East has caused widespread travel disruption, including airspace closures, delayed and cancelled flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel plans may be affected, even if your destination is not in the Middle East. Before you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check travel advice for any countries or territories you are transiting through"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for the latest updates from your airline or tour operator"]},{"k":"li","s":["review your travel insurance policy for coverage"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information and sign up for travel advice email alerts"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/south-korea/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of South Korea’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in South Korea set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["South Korean Embassy in the UK","https://overseas.mofa.go.kr/gb-en/index.do"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter South Korea as a tourist for up to 90 days, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ after the date you are leaving South Korea."]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter South Korea on a long-term visa, your passport should have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can enter South Korea for up to 90 days for short-term business or tourism. You must have an onward or return ticket. It’s illegal to be employed in South Korea while visiting visa-free, whether as a teacher or in any other capacity."]},{"k":"p","s":["South Korea operates an electronic travel authorisation system called K-ETA. Anyone eligible for visa-free entry to South Korea is usually required to get K-ETA approval before departure. However, British nationals travelling visa-free to South Korea are temporarily exempt from requiring a K-ETA until December 31, 2026. Further information about the K-ETA exemption can be found on the ",["K-ETA notice board","https://www.k-eta.go.kr/portal/board/viewboardlist.do?tmpltNm=notice&locale=EN"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need to apply for a K-ETA, you should ensure that you apply through the Korean government’s ",["official K-ETA website","https://www.k-eta.go.kr/portal/apply/index.do"],". Other sites offering K-ETA application services are generally scams. It can take up to 72 hours for K-ETA approval to be granted."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling for any purpose other than short-term business or tourism, check visa requirements with the South Korean Embassy in the UK."]},{"k":"p","s":["For those in South Korea on a work visa, all employment changes must be authorised by Korean Immigration."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Re-entry permits for long-term visa holders"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most foreign nationals in South Korea on long-term visas are allowed to re-enter South Korea within one year of departure without the need for a re-entry permit. Check with the ",["Korea Immigration Service","https://www.visa.go.kr/openPage.do?MENU_ID=10101&LANG_TYPE=EN"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are resident and intend to spend more than a year outside of South Korea, in most cases, you must apply for a multiple re-entry permit via the ",["Hi Korea website","https://www.hikorea.go.kr/Main.pt"]," before departure. If you require a re-entry permit, engage early with the immigration authorities and apply for a re-entry permit at least 4 working days ahead of any planned travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Visas for working as an English teacher"]},{"k":"p","s":["To get a visa to teach English in South Korea, you must have a 3-year university degree. A Teaching English as a Foreign Language (TEFL) qualification alone is not enough. If you are found to have a teaching visa by deception, you will be detained and deported."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals teaching English in South Korea have sometimes found living and working conditions to be below their expectation or have had difficulties getting the correct visas and residence permits. Some also report more serious problems such as breach of contract, confiscation of passport, payment being withheld and inadequate insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check all terms and conditions of your employment carefully. If possible, speak to other teachers from the place where you plan to work before accepting any offer. If you are in South Korea and in need of assistance, you should contact the ",["British Embassy in Seoul","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-embassy-seoul"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry declaration form"]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals entering South Korea are required to submit an entry declaration form (arrivals card) to the immigration officer upon arrival. Passengers may submit an e-Arrival card online in advance instead of submitting a paper form to the immigration officers."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can submit the e-Arrival card within 72 hours (3 days) before your arrival in Korea. There is no fee to submit the e-Arrival card. Travellers should visit the ",["e-Arrival card website","https://www.e-arrivalcard.go.kr/portal/main/index.do"]," for further details on the e-Arrival card submission process. Paper entry declaration forms will still be available."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health screening"]},{"k":"p","s":["All travellers arriving in South Korea from ‘Strict Quarantine Inspection Required Areas’ (including those who have transited in a ‘Strict Quarantine Inspection Required Area’) need to submit a health questionnaire, either through the pre-entry Q-Code system or by completing a paper-based questionnaire on arrival in South Korea. Travellers arriving in South Korea from ‘Quarantine Inspection Required Areas’ who exhibit symptoms must also submit a Q-Code or paper-based health questionnaire."]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK is currently designated as a ‘Quarantine Inspection Required Area’, meaning that if you have any symptoms of illness you must submit a Q-Code or paper-based health questionnaire on arrival."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers should check the full list of ",["Quarantine Inspection Required Areas","https://qcode.kdca.go.kr/qco/bbs/BD_selectBbsList.do?q_bbsSn=1016"]," prior to travel, as the countries on the lists change frequently. If you need to submit a questionnaire, you should also review the ",["Q-Code submission process","https://qcode.kdca.go.kr/qco/guide.do"],". Failure to complete required health screenings could result in a fine of up to KRW 10 million."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s South Korea guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/120/korea-south#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of South Korea","https://www.customs.go.kr/english/cm/cntnts/cntntsView.do?mi=8069&cntntsId=2743"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in South Korea"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in South Korea, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["The level of tension and the security situation on the Korean Peninsula can change with little notice. Tensions can rise after missile tests by North Korea and during the regular South Korean-US military exercises, which take place throughout the year. Follow the advice of local authorities and keep up to date with developments, which will be reported on news broadcasts."]},{"k":"p","s":["The demilitarised zone (DMZ) separates North Korea and South Korea. Peace has been maintained under an armistice agreement, but no formal peace treaty has ever been signed. If you’re in the area of the DMZ, you should exercise caution and follow the advice of the local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["National service"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a British male of Korean origin whose name appears on the Korean family register, you may be liable for military service even if you are travelling on your British passport."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Public demonstrations in South Korea are common, particularly at times of elevated political tensions. These gatherings are mostly peaceful and well-policed. Be aware that under Korean law, it is illegal for foreign nationals to take part in political activities when in the country. While in South Korea, pay attention to media reporting on political tensions and planned demonstrations, follow the advice of local authorities, and avoid large public gatherings."]},{"k":"h","s":["Civil emergency exercises and advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["South Korean authorities sometimes hold civil emergency exercises. You’ll hear sirens to mark the start of the exercise. All vehicles must stop and sometimes people will have to descend into designated metro stations or basements. You do not need to participate but do follow any instructions from officials during these exercises."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Contingency planning"]},{"k":"p","s":["The government’s Emergency Ready App, available on ",["iOS","https://apps.apple.com/kr/app/emergency-ready-app/id6748374479"]," and ",["Android","https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=kr.or.klid.newengsafekorea2025"],", explains the possible civil emergency alerts which would be pushed to your mobile in an emergency."]},{"k":"p","s":["As part of your own contingency planning, make sure you have easy access to your passport and other important documents such as nationality documents and birth and marriage certificates, as well as any essential medication. Consider saving the ",["contact details for the embassy","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-embassy-seoul"]," so that you can access them quickly if needed. Make sure to share your contact details with your family and friends."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime against foreigners is rare but there are occasional thefts. Take extra care of passports, credit cards and money in crowded areas and in areas visited by foreigners, such as Itaewon."]},{"k":"p","s":["While most reported crimes are thefts, there have been cases of assault, including sexual assault, particularly around bars and nightlife areas. Take care when travelling alone at night and only use legitimate taxis or public transport."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is a legal requirement to carry some form of identification, but people are rarely asked to show it."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re convicted of possession, use or trafficking of illegal drugs you can face a long jail sentence and heavy fines. This applies even to personal use of small amounts of marijuana. British nationals have been detained solely on the basis of drug tests."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in South Korea, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and read the ",["Korea Tourism Organization’s driving in Korea guidance","https://english.visitkorea.or.kr/svc/contents/contentsView.do?vcontsId=140664&menuSn=480"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both the ",["1949 international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car when you drive in South Korea. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The police take the position that car and motorbike drivers are at fault in accidents involving cyclists or pedestrians. If you injure someone in an accident, you are likely to face criminal charges and heavy penalties, even if guilt is not proved."]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal limit for alcohol in South Korea is less than half the limit in England, and penalties for drink-driving include prison and fines."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taxi drivers tend to speak little or no English. It is helpful to have your destination written in Korean – if possible with a map."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["If there is a natural disaster, or the threat of one, the South Korean government will publish updates in Korean and English to the Natural Disaster Safety Portal."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government’s Emergency Ready App, available on ",["iOS","https://apps.apple.com/gb/app/emergency-ready-app/id826120919"]," and ",["Android","https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=kr.go.nema.disasteralert_eng"],", explains the possible alerts which would be pushed to your mobile."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Typhoons"]},{"k":"p","s":["The typhoon season normally runs from June to November. Monitor the progress of approaching storms with the Korea Meteorological Administration or call 131 in Korea to get an accurate weather forecast in English. Always follow any advice given by the local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding and landslides"]},{"k":"p","s":["South Korea has heavy rainfall across the country during the summer rainy season, usually in June and July. Torrential rain may cause flooding near rivers and creeks, including in built-up areas. Flash floods are common in areas downstream from large reservoirs or rivers, even after relatively short periods of intense rainfall. Landslides are possible in hilly and mountainous areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor forecasts for heavy rainfall with the Korea Meteorological Administration and follow any advice given by the local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Strong earthquakes are unusual in South Korea but do happen. Most earthquakes in South Korea are relatively weak. The Korea Meteorological Administration publishes information on earthquakes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read up on the any guidance from local authorities on safety procedures in an earthquake and check the safety tips from the Seoul Metropolitan Government."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Forest fires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Forest fires may occur in South Korea. Pay attention to warnings from local authorities and follow any safety instructions that they issue. Korean-language emergency alerts will automatically be sent to your mobile phone if you are in an affected area, and English-language translations of emergency alerts can be accessed on the National Disaster and Safety Portal and in the ",["Emergency Ready App","https://agent.safekorea.go.kr/idsiSCH/era_pop.jsp"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can track the location and progress of fires through the Korea Forest Service website in ",["English","https://fd.forest.go.kr/ffas/pubConn/movePage/english.do"]," and ",["Korean","https://fd.forest.go.kr/ffas/index.jsp"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 119 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for South Korea","https://www.travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/120/south-korea#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in South Korea","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/120/south-korea#General_Information"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["insect and tick bites"]},{"k":"li","s":["tick-borne encephalitis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Air pollution, including yellow dust pollution, is common, especially during spring months. Follow local media reporting and check the ",["Korean Meteorological Administration","https://www.kma.go.kr/neng/index.do"]," website. On days when concentrations are high, most residents will stay indoors or use face masks outside. It’s also important to drink plenty of water."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["South Korean customs authorities allow you to bring small amounts of medication for your personal use, if it is kept in carry-on baggage. Take an English language prescription from your doctor at home for both your prescription drugs and non-prescription medicines. Consult the website of the ",["South Korean Ministry of Food and Drug Safety","https://www.mfds.go.kr/eng/index.do"]," before you travel to South Korea."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in South Korea"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical and dental care in South Korea is usually of a good standard, but can be expensive. Staff may not speak English. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need to stay in a South Korean hospital, particularly if your condition is severe, the hospital may ask you to bring a guardian or ‘bohoja’ to assist you with basic care needs such as trips to the bathroom, washing and exercise. It is possible to find agencies who will provide a caregiver or ‘ganbyungin’ for a fee, but these caregivers generally do not speak English. If you know that you may need to enter a Korean hospital, you should try to organise a guardian such as a friend or relative in advance."]},{"k":"p","s":["The South Korean Ministry of Health and Welfare (MOHW) maintains an ",["online database","https://www.e-gen.or.kr/egen/holiday_medical.do?emergencyViewYn=Y"]," (in Korean) of emergency services at available medical centres nationwide."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in South Korea","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/south-korea-doctors"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in South Korea","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-south-korea"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medical tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling to South Korea for elective treatment, such as cosmetic surgery or a dental procedure, consider that no medical procedure is risk-free. Make sure that your travel health insurance covers complications that may arise and repatriation to the UK if required."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in South Korea"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 119"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 119"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 112"]},{"k":"h","s":["English language support"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Korea Tourism Organisation (KTO) operates a travel hotline to provide assistance in multiple languages, including English. The hotline also offers interpretation services, including support for three-way calls (e.g. between British nationals, the hotline and emergency services) from 7am to midnight. Call 1330 to contact the travel hotline."]},{"k":"p","s":["Remote interpretation services may be helpful in the case of emergency or out of hours support. The following call centres offer interpretation support, including three-way calls, to foreigners in South Korea:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Dasan Call Centre (+82 2 120) – available 9am to 6pm Monday-Friday"]},{"k":"li","s":["Danuri Call Centre (1577 1366) – available 24/7"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=South%20Korea"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=South%20Korea"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=South%20Korea"]," in South Korea"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in South Korea","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-guide-for-south-korea"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in South Korea","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/south-korea-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/south-korea/british-embassy-seoul"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/south-korea/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in South Korea","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-south-korea"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":19890,"change":"Updated information about submitting e-Arrivals cards when arriving in Korea (‘Entry requirements’ page)."},"https://theconversation.com/microsoft-outage-shows-that-big-tech-cant-be-treated-as-too-big-to-fail-296599":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"ca2cf063caa74c392f8af33fcb2895a2bc6310bfe9946132583542cf80fa2a7e","read":"https://theconversation.com/microsoft-outage-shows-that-big-tech-cant-be-treated-as-too-big-to-fail-296599","bytes":178214,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Microsoft outage shows that big tech can’t be treated as too big to fail","by":[{"n":"Andrew Cullen","r":"Guest Research Fellow, School of Computing and Information Systems, The University of Melbourne"}],"pub":"2026-11-16T01:27:20Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["When a ",["massive outage","https://theconversation.com/microsoft-has-suffered-a-global-outage-a-tech-expert-explains-what-went-wrong-296588"]," hit Microsoft late last week, much of the digital world ground to a halt."]},{"k":"p","s":["The outage wiped out key Microsoft services including Outlook, Teams and Copilot, which are used by more than ",["430 million people around the world","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c6rrg51rkz09o"],". As email and internal communications froze, the operations of ",["governments","https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c6vg2ljjpj32o"]," and ",["businesses went dark","https://www.tomshardware.com/tech-industry/data-centers/microsoft-365-outage-leads-to-chlorine-gas-poisoning-of-15-hotel-guests-email-warning-system-fails-40-first-responders-deployed-for-triage-four-hospitalized"]," alongside them, triggering an economic paralysis that could ",["cost billions of dollars","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/14/microsoft-deeply-sorry-for-global-disruption-that-could-have-billion-dollar-impact-on-australia"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["While the global economy absorbs the brunt of this paralysis, Microsoft faces both a severe reputational hit and contractual penalties that could reach up to ",["US$800 million per day","https://edition.cnn.com/2026/11/12/business/live-news/microsoft-global-outage-intl-hnk?post-id=cmwf6e7el00003b6txhzlcvvg&t=1794587807347"]," for services they failed to deliver."]},{"k":"p","s":["Such a catastrophic outage shows just how precarious our modern digital infrastructure is. It depends on a handful of big tech companies, which have essentially become too big to fail. So how did we end up in this situation? And is there a way out?"]},{"k":"h","s":["Digital dependency"]},{"k":"p","s":["The initial source of Microsoft’s failure was incredibly innocuous. Data centres usually share the load of user demands across systems all over the world. However, last week, a small configuration change caused the company to ",["lose control of some of their computers","https://time.com/article/2026/11/13/microsoft-outage-worldwide-disruption-teams-outlook-emails/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unable to share the load, these computers dropped user requests onto other systems, overwhelming them and producing more outages. This pattern repeated over and over again until the company lost almost complete control of their network."]},{"k":"p","s":["Worse, disconnected user devices – phones, email clients and business systems – all automatically tried to reconnect at once, ",["crashing Microsoft’s systems all over again","https://www.sciencemediacentre.org/expert-reaction-to-microsoft-outage"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Historically, a tech outage might affect a single company. But the reason Microsoft’s outage could impact millions of people comes down to a business revolution that silently took place ",["over 20 years ago","https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/1506409.1506419"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Software was once something that was sold to companies once for an upfront cost. In this model, purchasers held great power – only buying new versions if the update justified the expense."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet, these upfront expenses also scared consumers off. Drawing inspiration from telecommunications, gyms and real estate leasing, the tech industry transitioned to renting access to their products, creating what is now known as “ ",["software as a service","https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/1506409.1506419"],"”."]},{"k":"p","s":["In theory, ",["everyone profited from this model","https://link.springer.com/content/pdf/10.1057/palgrave.dam.3640007.pdf"],". Software vendors could bank more reliable cash flow, and customers could transition to regular smaller payments, rather than stumping up for large upfront costs."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ultimately, this change shifted the balance of power towards tech companies. Instead of purchasing features they needed, consumers handed the keys to their operational kingdoms to the “software as service” providers, and locked themselves into highly expensive long-term contracts in the process."]},{"k":"h","s":["Too big to fail"]},{"k":"p","s":["The global financial crisis in 2008 introduced the world to the idea of too big to fail. When it hit, the public was left to pick up the pieces of banks that had become too systemically important to be allowed to fail."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unfortunately, it appears we haven’t really learned those lessons. Instead, we’ve spent the last few years living through a slow-motion version of that with the tech industry. Centralisation, consolidation and unchecked monopolies have left our digital lives, our businesses and our governments in an incredibly precarious place."]},{"k":"p","s":["On one level or another, almost everything on the internet goes through ",["Google","https://outagecost.com/gcp-outages"],", Microsoft, ",["Meta","https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2021/oct/05/facebook-outage-what-went-wrong-and-why-did-it-take-so-long-to-fix"],", ",["Amazon Web Services","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2025-10-21/amazon-web-services-aws-outage-explained/105917274"]," or ",["CrowdStrike","https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/article/2024/jul/19/microsoft-windows-pcs-outage-blue-screen-of-death"]," – all of which have had major outages over recent years."]},{"k":"p","s":["These big tech giants earned our trust by providing unified, seemingly invincible infrastructure. But the convenience that comes with centralisation holds a trap."]},{"k":"p","s":["Unlike the banking sector in 2008, when these tech titans fail, they don’t need to ask governments to bail them out. Instead, their centrality forces the entire digital economy to bear the costs of their outage."]},{"k":"h","s":["Developing digital sovereignty"]},{"k":"p","s":["Escaping the reliance on a few tech giants for our national infrastructure, businesses and citizens’ data has spurned the push for so-called ",["digital sovereignty","https://www.europarl.europa.eu/RegData/etudes/BRIE/2020/651992/EPRS_BRI(2020)651992_EN.pdf"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Europe is leading the way on this","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-14/microsoft-outage-and-cloud-providers-tech-risk-in-australia/107383316"],". By actively funding decentralised cloud infrastructure and homegrown software, governments are ensuring that an American tech failure cannot knock out a local hospital."]},{"k":"p","s":["The world must adopt a similar blueprint. Australia, in particular, is well placed to grasp the opportunities that digital sovereignty brings. We already have the raw engineering talent. Companies such as Atlassian, Apromore, Airwallex and Canva have proven we can build world-class digital tools."]},{"k":"p","s":["If governments strategically invested in local tech ecosystems, they wouldn’t just be buying digital insurance. They would drive much-needed market competition, dilute the power of big-tech monopolies and spread out systemic risks – ensuring that a single point of failure could never bring the economy to its knees."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is not to say we should divest ourselves of any connection to big-tech platforms, which do and will continue to provide useful services. But if our entire global economy continues to rely on a handful of too-big-to-fail digital monopolies, we will have no one but ourselves to blame when our screens inevitably go black again."]}],"chars":5189},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/el-salvador":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"4342d1193db4118264e1621014b3e55bb275f75b2d30e68f00c092d17ad21965","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/el-salvador","bytes":60678,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"El Salvador travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-02-05T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-05T14:10:46+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/el-salvador/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of El Salvador’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in El Salvador set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Salvadoran Embassy in the UK","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/foreign-embassies-in-the-uk"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter El Salvador, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the day you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can travel to El Salvador for tourism or business for up to 180 days without a visa."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can extend your stay by contacting the ",["General Directorate of Migration and Immigration","https://www.migracion.gob.sv/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer (to work or study, for business travel or for other reasons), you must meet the Salvadoran government’s entry requirements. Check which type of visa or work permit you need with the ",["Salvadoran Embassy in the UK","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/foreign-embassies-in-the-uk"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you overstay your visa, you may have to pay a fine before leaving the country."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you need a visa, contact the ",["Salvadoran Embassy in the UK","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/foreign-embassies-in-the-uk"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travelling between El Salvador, Guatemala, Honduras and Nicaragua"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can travel between El Salvador, Guatemala, Honduras and Nicaragua for up to 90 days without a visa. Read the travel advice for:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["Guatemala","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/guatemala/entry-requirements"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Honduras","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/honduras/entry-requirements"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Nicaragua","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nicaragua/entry-requirements"]]},{"k":"p","s":["The 90-day period starts when you enter any of these countries and does not restart when you cross borders. You’ll have to go through immigration checks at borders."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re expelled from one of these countries, you’re also excluded from the other 3. If you overstay, you may get a fine."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter El Salvador, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s El Salvador guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/72/el-salvador#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["El Salvador has introduced additional health measures in response to the Ebola outbreak."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers who have been in, or transited through, Angola, Burundi, Ethiopia, Kenya, the Central African Republic, the Democratic Republic of the Congo, Rwanda or Uganda in the 21 days before arriving in El Salvador are subject to a 21-day quarantine requirement for observation and health monitoring. You may be refused entry if you cannot meet the quarantine requirement."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have recently travelled through one of the listed countries, contact El Salvador’s Ministry of Health or your nearest Salvadoran embassy before you travel to check how the quarantine requirement applies to you."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of El Salvador. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Taking money into El Salvador"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 US dollars or more."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transit fee for Indian and African nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["Indian nationals or nationals from any African country travelling through El Salvador must pay a 1,130 US dollar fee. See ",["transit fee for Indian and African nationals","https://ayuda.avianca.com/hc/en-us/articles/19744371443355"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["British dual nationals will not have to pay the fee if they travel on their British passport."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in El Salvador"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in El Salvador, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid demonstrations and do not engage in any political activity."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal for foreign nationals to engage in political activities such as public demonstrations in El Salvador. If you participate in demonstrations, you may be detained and deported. Avoid large gatherings or demonstrations and be cautious in public areas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Security in El Salvador has improved considerably with significant reductions in crime. However, travellers should remain cautious as the risks of violent and petty crime still exist."]},{"k":"hs","s":["State of exception (emergency)"]},{"k":"p","s":["El Salvador’s government declared a state of exception (emergency) in response to a sharp rise in gang-related murders. The state of exception started in 2022 and has remained in place since. The murder rate has fallen significantly, but the authorities are concerned the gangs could regroup."]},{"k":"p","s":["The state of exception gives police additional powers, resulting in a much higher number of arrests, sometimes without much evidence. It also allows police to detain people for much longer before trial. Many ordinary legal safeguards have also been weakened or removed. For example, joint legal hearings for over 100 people are common."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some embassies have struggled to get consular access to their citizens. If you’re arrested, the El Salvador government may not allow the British Embassy to give you consular assistance or make sure you receive legal representation. Mistreatment and human rights violations, sometimes resulting in death, happen in detention facilities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Security operations and gang-related violence do not usually affect tourists and visitors. Security operations have taken place across the country, particularly in Soyapango, Ilopango, Mejicanos, San Martin and San Marcos."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2022 the Salvadoran Legislative Assembly designated gang members as terrorists and established harsher penalties for them. Government communications and social media posts now sometimes refer to suspected gang members as terrorists."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Robberies and violent assaults"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been isolated attacks on tourists, including robberies, carjackings and violent assaults."]},{"k":"p","s":["Within San Salvador, the areas of Santa Elena, San Benito and Maquilishuat have better security, as do most of the larger shopping malls."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid walking alone or on remote trails. It may be safer to travel with others or go on a tour with a reputable company. Take extra care in more deprived areas of towns and cities and those less visited by tourists. Follow local advice on where the safer areas are."]},{"k":"p","s":["Withdraw money from ATMs in shopping centres or change money in hotels or banks. Do not withdraw a lot of money at one time or use ATMs at night or in badly lit areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Protect yourself by:"]},{"k":"li","s":["keeping valuables, including your passport, in a hotel safe if possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["being aware of pickpockets at bus stations, airports, tourist sites and on public transport"]},{"k":"li","s":["not wearing expensive jewellery, particularly at airports, and only carrying a small amount of cash"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re driving, take the following precautions:"]},{"k":"li","s":["take extra care at junctions, where armed robbers often target stationary traffic"]},{"k":"li","s":["stick to main roads and avoid unsurfaced roads, as you’re at greater risk in remote areas with fewer police patrols"]},{"k":"li","s":["always lock doors and keep windows closed. If you’re robbed, do not resist the attackers or take any action that puts you at greater risk"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have questions on security, contact the El Salvador tourist police:"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: +503 2224 2705"]},{"k":"p","s":["Email: info@politurelsalvador.com"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Buses and taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Public buses (repainted old US school buses) are not safe due to petty crime. Private intercity buses are generally safer, although crime can also happen on these. Only use reputable coach companies. For shorter trips within towns and cities, take radio-dispatched, pre-booked or hotel taxis operated by reputable companies. Do not use unofficial taxis, as there remains a small risk of kidnapping."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criminal kidnapping"]},{"k":"p","s":["The risk of kidnapping to foreigners or visitors is relatively low, however, you might wish to share your location or plans with a trusted person, particularly if taking public transport or a taxi."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Scam artists target foreign visitors and residents. Scams come in many forms and can cause great financial loss. Warn your friends and family to be sceptical if they’re asked to transfer funds to you in El Salvador. Tell them to contact you to check you’ve made this request."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["The police may ask you for ID. They may detain you if they suspect you are a gang member. Always carry a copy of the photo page of your passport to prove your identity."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["The official currencies of El Salvador are the US dollar and bitcoin. Bitcoins may not be accepted everywhere. If you’re considering using bitcoins, make sure you understand the risks involved. Also make sure you can access US dollars if needed."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is almost impossible to change British pounds anywhere in El Salvador, so you should bring a mixture of cash and travellers cheques in US dollars."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many smaller restaurants, bars and shops do not accept 50 and 100 US dollar notes. You can exchange these notes at a bank. Bring smaller denominations with you if possible."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regular ATMs and bitcoin ATMs are widely available, particularly in San Salvador and La Libertad. Tell your bank of your travel plans to avoid your card being blocked."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Crowded events"]},{"k":"p","s":["In May 2023, at least 12 people died and more than 500 were injured during a football match at the Cuscatlán Stadium, due to overcrowding. If you’re attending events in crowded places and large gatherings, follow the advice of the local authorities and maintain a high level of security awareness."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are severe penalties for drug use and trafficking in El Salvador. Prisons are overcrowded and violent."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex marriage, civil unions and adoption are illegal in El Salvador. Although same-sex relationships are not illegal, there is limited public acceptance of them or people with diverse gender identities, and there are no laws that explicitly protect LGBT+ people from discrimination. Public displays of affection between people of the same-sex, particularly outside of San Salvador, could result in verbal and physical harassment, discrimination and potentially violence"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Landmines and unexploded weapons"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a small risk of unexploded weapons, such as landmines, in remote areas. If you’re going off-road, take local advice and avoid such areas if warned."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Swimming on the Pacific coast can be dangerous due to strong undertows. The currents around La Bocana de San Diego are particularly treacherous. Several people have drowned in recent years. There are very few or no lifeguards. You should avoid swimming on isolated beaches, especially after consuming alcohol."]},{"k":"p","s":["Rivers tend to be contaminated and unsafe to swim or bathe in."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in El Salvador, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in El Salvador for the first 90 days after you arrive. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"],". El Salvador does not accept the international driving permit."]},{"k":"p","s":["After 90 days, you must get an El Salvador driving licence. Before you can apply for a licence, you must already have a temporary residency permit. You’ll need to ",["have your UK licence certified (‘Homologación Licencia Extranjera’)","https://www.sertracen.com.sv/index.php/homologacion-licencia-extranjera"]," as part of the application process."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience or a higher minimum age."]},{"k":"p","s":["Car insurance is essential. If you’re involved in an accident, call 911 to reach the national police or fire brigade. Wait for the police to arrive."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards vary. Lane discipline is poor."]},{"k":"p","s":["Roads between the main tourist locations in El Salvador are of a good or acceptable standard. Thieves sometimes steal manhole covers, leaving large holes in the road. In more isolated locations, roads are unsurfaced and 4-wheel-drive vehicles are necessary."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Crossing borders"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take particular care when driving to or from the border with Guatemala. There have been violent attacks on vehicles, particularly on the Guatemalan side of the border. Criminals often target vehicles with El Salvador number plates. It’s better to cross borders in the morning, giving you time to reach your destination before dark. Borders sometimes close in the early evening. Private bus companies are considered safer than public buses for crossing borders."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rainy season"]},{"k":"p","s":["The rainy season normally runs from June to November – the same time as the hurricane season in the Caribbean. During the rainy season you can expect frequent, heavy rain, thunderstorms and possible tropical depressions. Landslides and flooding can affect roads. Mountain areas are particularly vulnerable to landslides."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor local and international weather updates from the ",["Dirección General de Observatorio de Amenazas y Recursos Naturales","https://www.snet.gob.sv/"]," (in Spanish), the World Meteorological Organization and the US National Hurricane Center."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hurricanes"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["FCDO guidance on tropical cyclones","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"]," for advice about what to do if you’re caught in a hurricane."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Volcanic eruptions"]},{"k":"p","s":["El Salvador has active volcanoes, at least 6 of which are monitored."]},{"k":"p","s":["Get local advice before climbing volcanoes in El Salvador and monitor local media for updates on increased volcanic activity. Check the Directorate General of Civil Protection for volcano warnings. It’s safer to climb volcanoes or walk in remote areas during daylight hours with a tour guide."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent minor earth tremors and occasional earthquakes in El Salvador. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],". If you’re staying in a hotel, read their earthquake instructions."]},{"k":"p","s":["See the ",["Ministry of the Environment and Natural Resources","https://www.ambiente.gob.sv/"]," for information on El Salvador earthquakes."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tsunamis"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of tsunamis in coastal areas. See ",["tsunamis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire risk increases during the dry season, particularly in San Salvador. During especially hot and dry periods a single spark or flame can start a wildfire. Report fires to the emergency services immediately."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 911 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccination recommendations for El Salvador","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/72/el-salvador#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in El Salvador","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/72/el-salvador"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of El Salvador. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of contaminated drinking water. Bottled water is inexpensive and widely available."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries. UK prescriptions cannot be used in El Salvador. To find a pharmacy (‘farmacia’) look for one of the big national chains such as Farmacia San Nicolas, Farmacias UNO or Farmacias Economicas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in El Salvador"]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities outside San Salvador are usually basic. State-run hospitals are generally understaffed, underfunded and ill-equipped. Use private clinics and hospitals whenever possible. Some hospitals may be reluctant to treat you until they know you have medical insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation. Always carry a copy of your insurance cover. Most medical staff speak only a little English."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in El Salvador","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/list-of-medical-facilities-in-el-salvador"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in El Salvador"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 911 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Tourist police"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: +503 2224 2705"]},{"k":"p","s":["Email: info@politurelsalvador.com"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=El%20Salvador"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=El%20Salvador"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=El%20Salvador"]," in El Salvador"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in El Salvador","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/death-pack-for-el-salvador"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in El Salvador","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/prisoners-pack-for-el-salvador"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/el-salvador/british-embassy-san-salvador"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/el-salvador/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in El Salvador","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-el-salvador"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":19713,"change":"Updated information about visa requirements when travelling between El Salvador, Guatemala, Honduras and Nicaragua ('Entry requirements' page)."},"https://theconversation.com/missing-ambassadors-inexperienced-appointees-is-washington-dropping-the-diplomatic-ball-293487":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"8a24d7c2511174ebf629a367f92f3b409eb21a6c4c2591e64f31f5c1bdab1151","read":"https://theconversation.com/missing-ambassadors-inexperienced-appointees-is-washington-dropping-the-diplomatic-ball-293487","bytes":181036,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Missing ambassadors, inexperienced appointees – is Washington dropping the diplomatic ball?","by":[{"n":"Donald Heflin","r":"Executive Director of the Edward R. Murrow Center and Senior Fellow of Diplomatic Practice, The Fletcher School, Tufts University"}],"pub":"2026-10-07T12:10:02Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Just before leaving town on Sept. 30, 2026, ",["U.S. senators confirmed 10 new ambassadors","https://www.senate.gov/pagelayout/legislative/one_item_and_teasers/nom_confc.htm"],". Among those nodded through before Congress closed for an extended midterm recess were new U.S. ambassadors for Kenya, Nicaragua, Malaysia and Kyrgyzstan."]},{"k":"p","s":["That’s commendable – many of those countries hold geographical or strategic importance for U.S. diplomacy. But it still leaves ",["92 out of 196 ambassador jobs","https://afsa.org/list-ambassadorial-appointments"]," currently unfilled. In some of those cases, the White House has not sent names to Capitol Hill despite the second Trump administration being a year and a half into the job. In others, the Senate, which is controlled by the same party as the White House, hasn’t acted on the names put forward."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regardless of the reason, as a ",["former ambassador and an expert in the process of diplomacy","https://sites.tufts.edu/murrowcenter/leadership/"],", I find the current vacancies concerning. Among those embassies still without a top person in place are key partners for the U.S. – countries that Washington needs to achieve its security, economic and strategic objectives."]},{"k":"p","s":["What makes these vacancies more worrying, in my view, is that they come amid other concerning developments in the State Department’s staffing of embassies."]},{"k":"h","s":["Politicizing diplomacy"]},{"k":"p","s":["Chief among them are the ",["high percentage of politically appointed ambassadors","https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2026/08/06/trump-fills-ambassador-posts-with-more-donors-loyalists-than-any-recent-president/"]," relative to positions filled by career diplomats – that is, senior foreign service officers, usually with at least 20 years of diplomatic experience."]},{"k":"p","s":["Though many countries send politicians abroad as ambassadors, America’s diplomatic service is unique in two ways. The percentage of U.S. ambassadors who are political appointees – those who haven’t followed a career civil service path – is ",["higher than comparative countries","https://doi.org/10.1093/ia/iiae116"]," across the world. Second, those political appointees are ",["often donors with little to no government experience","https://theconversation.com/trumps-insistence-on-personal-loyalty-from-ambassadors-could-crimp-us-foreign-policy-273087"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The practice has existed for decades, but in recent years the ",["number of political appointees has increased","https://afsa.org/appointments-barack-obama"],". During the Obama administration, the percentage of political appointees was around 30%. The number rose to around 40% in the first Trump administration and the subsequent Biden administration."]},{"k":"p","s":["But in Trump’s second term, some ",["80% of names the White House has sent","https://afsa.org/appointments-donald-j-trump-2nd-term"]," to the Senate have been political."]},{"k":"p","s":["And many of the people Trump has put forward don’t appear to have the credentials usually associated with holding important diplomatic positions. Rather, ",["many are friends, associates or donors","https://www.washingtonpost.com/national-security/2026/08/06/trump-fills-ambassador-posts-with-more-donors-loyalists-than-any-recent-president/"]," to Trump, often with little overseas experience or knowledge of the country they are going to."]},{"k":"p","s":["Lee Lipton, ",["ambassador to a key ally in the Philippines","https://ph.usembassy.gov/ambassador-lee-lipton/"],", is owner of a restaurant in Palm Beach – Florida Benny’s on the Beach – a member of Trump’s Mar-a-Lago Club and a contributor to his political campaign. The ",["ambassador to Greece","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/01/04/world/europe/kimberly-guilfoyle-trump-greece-ambassador.html"]," is Kimberly Guilfoyle, a former Trump adviser and ex-fiancée of his son Donald Jr."]},{"k":"p","s":["The system of political appointees has always had an element of handing ambassadorships to friends and supporters. But what has changed under Trump is the range of positions now available. In the past, ambassadors to key countries like Chile, Israel, Peru, the Philippines, Turkey and Egypt, for example, have almost always been career appointees. This has changed under the second Trump administration."]},{"k":"p","s":["Appointing noncareer diplomats to small, faraway nations has the additional problem that the chosen individual may not actually spend much time there. The rule of thumb has long been that ambassadors should spend no more than one month every year back in the United States. But that is compromised if a noncareer diplomat with expansive business ties in the U.S. is selected."]},{"k":"h","s":["The role of a deputy"]},{"k":"p","s":["A closely related problem is the State Department’s handling of an ambassador’s second in command, their ",["deputy chiefs of missions","https://afsa.org/current-deputy-chiefs-mission"]," – DCMs for short – under Secretary of State Marco Rubio."]},{"k":"p","s":["During Trump’s first term in the White House, politically appointed ambassadors were often ",["encouraged to swap out the DCMs","https://theconversation.com/trumps-insistence-on-personal-loyalty-from-ambassadors-could-crimp-us-foreign-policy-273087"]," they inherited from their predecessors. It meant going through a long hiring process, leaving those key jobs unfilled for months."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2025, the State Department went further, canceling the assignments of senior officers ",["en route to take up embassy jobs","https://www.nbcwashington.com/news/national-international/trump-removes-nearly-30-career-diplomats-from-ambassadorial-positions/4032589/"]," and opening a new hiring process."]},{"k":"p","s":["It formed part of a Trump purge of what many MAGA Republicans ",["characterized as a “deep state” civil service","https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2025/dec/23/trump-administration-recalls-30-ambassadors-promote-loyal-diplomats"],". The reality is that DCMs ",["fill a critically important role","https://diplomaticacademy.us/2024/12/29/advice-for-political-ambassadors/"]," in helping political appointees navigate the bureaucracy and implement their policy ideas, as well as raising the occasional reality check."]},{"k":"p","s":["With more politically appointed ambassadors – some of them with no relevant experience – having an experienced DCM can be the difference between success and failure."]},{"k":"h","s":["Looking for other friends"]},{"k":"p","s":["When you put all of these personnel changes together, the result is the degradation of what was once seen as one of the most effective diplomatic services in the world."]},{"k":"p","s":["What makes this potentially more worrying is where the vacancies are. For example, Belarus and Bulgaria, neighbors to Russia and Ukraine, are without U.S. ambassadors. And important countries in the fight against terrorism or in geopolitical hot spots, such as Kuwait, Qatar and Mauritania, are in the same camp."]},{"k":"p","s":["Other countries still without ambassadors include Indonesia, Southeast Asia’s largest nation and the most populous Muslim-majority country in the world; key Middle East ally Egypt and nuclear power Pakistan; and nations the U.S. needs to help manage inward migration, such us Haiti and Guatemala."]},{"k":"p","s":["The problem of absent or inexperienced ambassadors goes both ways. It means Washington may not have a capable diplomatic figurehead in these countries to contact in times of need. There are also fewer avenues for host nations to successfully convey messages back to the U.S. administration."]},{"k":"p","s":["When faced with absent ambassadors, amateurish political appointees and deputy mission chiefs who are very junior or career appointees with short resumes, host countries may conclude that they aren’t seen as important to the U.S. and start looking elsewhere for friends."]},{"k":"p","s":["And the U.S. has hollowed out its ambassadorial corps at a time when it is facing growing international influence by the ",["likes of Russia","https://www.rand.org/nsrd/projects/russian-arms-sales-and-sanctions-compliance.html"],", ",["China","https://www.usglc.org/chinas-growing-influence-is-america-getting-left-behind/"]," and Iran – rival nations hoping to capitalize on a perceived diplomatic void left by Washington."]},{"k":"p","s":["For example, as the U.S. tries to ",["contain Beijing’s influence","https://www.brookings.edu/articles/a-framework-for-u-s-policy-toward-china-2/"]," in the Asia-Pacific region, Fiji, Indonesia and Laos remain without U.S. ambassadors. Similarly, China’s diplomatic relations with Pakistan – a former key security partner for Washington – have grown while the ambassadorial seat in Islamabad remains empty."]},{"k":"p","s":["And former Soviet states including Georgia and Kazakhstan don’t have U.S. ambassadors even as Russia President Vladimir Putin attempts to consolidate Moscow’s regional influence."]},{"k":"p","s":["In large areas of the world, such as Africa and the Pacific region, and in important areas of policy, the lights may be on in U.S. embassies, but nobody’s home. And that is a distinct problem for national security and strategic interests."]}],"chars":6999},"https://theconversation.com/while-californias-wealth-tax-failed-states-are-taking-other-steps-to-collect-more-revenue-from-the-rich-296103":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"8c3cb8db985d2e97e2763c79c6b079ecefac79923de99f0cbf418ecaa6dbb2c6","read":"https://theconversation.com/while-californias-wealth-tax-failed-states-are-taking-other-steps-to-collect-more-revenue-from-the-rich-296103","bytes":190698,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"While California’s wealth tax failed, states are taking other steps to collect more revenue from the rich","by":[{"n":"Allison Anna Tait","r":"Professor of Law, University of Richmond"}],"pub":"2026-11-12T13:41:41Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["State ",["efforts to tax the rich","https://itep.org/voters-pass-ballot-measures-to-raise-and-protect-revenue-tax-the-rich/"]," did relatively well in the 2026 midterm elections, following a series of state legislative moves in that direction in recent years."]},{"k":"p","s":["That might come as a surprise because a ",["majority of voters rejected","https://www.cbsnews.com/sanfrancisco/news/california-proposition-40-billionaire-wealth-tax-rejected-cbs-projects/"]," California’s ",["Proposition 40","https://calmatters.org/health/2026/11/california-election-2026-prop-40-41-42/"],". The much-publicized ballot initiative would have imposed a one-time 5% tax on the net worth of the state’s roughly 200 billionaires. Google co-founder Sergey Brin and several other billionaires ",["spent nearly $400 million","https://calmatters.org/politics/elections/2026/11/prop-40-billionaire-tax-defeated/"]," trying to persuade voters to reject it."]},{"k":"p","s":["Emmanuel Saez, a University of California, Berkeley economist who studies inequality and helped design Proposition 40, lamented the loss, saying: “ ",["Today oligarchy has won","https://ls.berkeley.edu/news/after-billionaire-tax-fails-economists-are-asking-%E2%80%98what%E2%80%99s-next%E2%80%99"],".”"]},{"k":"p","s":["As a ",["law professor","https://law.richmond.edu/faculty/atait/"]," who recently ",["wrote a book about wealth inequality","https://www.ucpress.edu/books/the-house-that-family-money-built/paper"],", I have been monitoring the results of these efforts aimed at taxing the rich. Despite Proposition 40’s failure, I think it’s important to observe that many Americans expressed support during the midterms for hiking income taxes on the rich, and to a lesser extent, taxes on the second – ",["or third or fourth","https://www.tiffanyhousefortlauderdale.com/blog/why-do-billionaires-buy-so-many-houses/"]," – homes the very wealthy possess."]},{"k":"h","s":["Taxing the rich at the ballot box"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taxing income is proving a more successful strategy than taxing wealth."]},{"k":"p","s":["Major changes to income taxes were ",["up for a vote in five states","https://www.newsweek.com/5-states-vote-for-major-changes-to-income-tax-12683305"]," during the midterms. Three of those ballot initiatives were proposals that sought to boost income tax rates on the rich or maintain those rates. All three prevailed."]},{"k":"p","s":[["In Washington state","https://mynorthwest.com/mynorthwest-politics/millionaires-tax-i-645-2/4286467"],", for example, voters backed a measure that will preserve ",["its new 9.9% income tax","https://washingtonstatestandard.com/2026/11/03/washington-voters-embracing-income-tax-on-high-earners/"]," on household income above $1 million. This “millionaire’s tax,” signed into law earlier in 2026, is the state’s first personal income tax."]},{"k":"p","s":["Meanwhile, ",["Colorado voters rejected Proposition 136","https://coloradosun.com/2026/11/06/proposition-136-results-amendment-87-income-tax-limit/"],", which would have capped the state’s income tax rate at 4.4%. They also ",["approved Amendment 87","https://coloradosun.com/2026/11/06/amendment-87-results-passes-graduated-income-tax/"],", a new graduated income tax that raises rates on households and businesses with incomes over $500,000."]},{"k":"p","s":["And even though California’s voters rejected Proposition 40, they did ",["approve Proposition 3","https://calmatters.org/california-voter-guide-2026/proposition-3-high-income-tax/"],". That measure makes permanent the income tax rates enacted in 2012 for the state’s highest earners, which were set to expire in 2031. The surcharges, adjusted annually for inflation, start at 10.3% for incomes of $360,000 and go up to a 12.3% surcharge for taxpayers earning over $721,000."]},{"k":"p","s":["And in August 2026, ",["Missouri voters overwhelmingly rejected a measure","https://mobudget.org/voters-resoundingly-reject-amendment-5/"]," that would have required the state’s lawmakers to eliminate its income tax. This would have meant losing ",["$8.5 billion in revenue","https://www.stlpr.org/government-politics-issues/2026-08-04/amendment-5-missouri-income-sales-tax"]," annually. The change would have let rich income taxpayers off the hook and replaced lost revenue through an increased sales tax that would have hit low-income taxpayers hardest."]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["two losses were in North Carolina and Iowa","https://www.desmoinesregister.com/story/news/politics/elections/2026/11/04/iowa-amendment-1-results-midterm-election-income-tax/92382820007/"],". Neither state voted directly on a tax to be levied on the rich. But both approved constitutional amendments that will make it harder for the state legislatures to enact these kinds of taxes in the future. North Carolina’s governor, Josh Stein, called the amendment in his state a “ ",["millionaire protection cap","https://www.carolinajournal.com/stein-warns-against-lowering-nc-constitutional-tax-cap/"],".”"]},{"k":"h","s":["State legislatures raising income tax rates on high earners"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ahead of the midterms, new taxes on the rich ",["introduced via state legislatures","https://www.ncsl.org/state-legislatures-news/details/everything-you-ever-wanted-to-know-about-wealth-taxes"],", rather than ballot initiatives, also emerged."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Maine, legislators voted in April 2026 for a tax surcharge of 1% on income over $1 million. The following month, Hawaiian lawmakers created a ",["new 13% income bracket","https://files.hawaii.gov/tax/news/announce/ann26-06.pdf"]," for single taxpayers earning above $500,000 or couples filing jointly who make over $1 million. This change is paired with a reduction in rates for lower-income brackets."]},{"k":"p","s":["And one month after that, Rhode Island enacted a ",["surcharge for millionaires’ income","https://itep.org/rhode-island-budget-millionaires-tax-ctc-social-security-conformity/"]," to be phased in over the next three years, reaching a maximum 3% rate."]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2009, New York became one of the first states to pass one of these ",["high-earner income taxes","https://www.forbes.com/sites/ashleaebeling/2019/04/09/new-yorks-temporary-millionaire-tax-extended-5-more-years/"],". ",["Washington, D.C., Massachusetts and Maryland","https://www.cbpp.org/research/state-budget-and-tax/states-that-raised-revenue-offer-brighter-roadmap-for-others"]," also enacted these “millionaire taxes” in 2022, 2023 and 2025, respectively."]},{"k":"h","s":["Taxing additional homes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Another way that state and local governments are boosting the tax revenue they get from wealthy constituents is by levying special taxes on pricey homes ",["that aren’t the owners’ primary residences","https://finance.yahoo.com/news/billionaires-own-most-homes-135805836.html?guccounter=1"],". These initiatives have succeeded both in state legislatures and voting booths."]},{"k":"p","s":["Montana lawmakers, in April 2025, approved a new ",["tiered property tax system","https://bozemanrealestate.group/blog/understanding-montana-property-taxes"],", which took effect on Jan. 1, 2026. It raised property tax rates on vacation homes and short-term rentals to 1.9%, while primary residences and qualifying long-term rentals pay lower, ",["tiered homestead rates","https://www.investopedia.com/terms/h/homestead-exemption.asp"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["New York City rolled out its “ ",["pied-à-terre tax","https://www.nyc.gov/site/finance/property/non-primary-residence-surcharge.page"],"” in July. The new tax imposes an annual surcharge of 0.8% to 1.3% on single-family homes valued at $5 million or more, and 4% to 6.5% on condos and co-ops valued at $1 million or more. The surcharge only applies to homes that are not a ",["primary residence","https://www.sullcrom.com/insights/memo/2026/July/New-NYC-Non-Primary-Residence-Tax"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Rhode Island has a similar property tax","https://www.wpri.com/target-12/taylor-swift-tax-goes-into-effect-in-rhode-island-heres-how-many-could-pay/"]," that took effect at the same time as New York City’s. It’s an annual surcharge of $2.50 for every $500 of assessed value above $1 million that applies to non-primary residences."]},{"k":"p","s":["And on Nov. 3, voters in Boulder, Colorado, approved a ",["residential vacancy tax","https://bouldercolorado.gov/news/city-boulder-voters-support-three-ballot-measures-nov-3-2026-election"]," on homes that sit empty more than half the year. The surcharge, which goes into effect in 2028, will be roughly $4,000 a year for each vacant property. It applies across the board, but homes that aren’t primary residences are the clear target."]},{"k":"p","s":["However, just west of Boulder in Crested Butte, Colorado, a ",["second-home tax","https://crestedbuttenews.com/2026/11/state-issues-cause-delay-for-local-election-results/"]," failed. So did an effort to levy a ",["similar surcharge","https://www.sd-cash-buyer.com/blog/san-diego-measure-a-vacant-homes-tax-rejection-2026-election-results/"]," in San Diego, California."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why income taxes are attractive to voters and lawmakers"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a good reason why taxing the income of rich people is easier to pull off than taxing their wealth: Income taxes are much ",["easier to calculate","https://itep.org/a-wealth-tax-might-be-easier-to-implement-than-you-think/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Income taxes can be based on annual income tax filings, whether state or federal. It requires no extra work to value someone’s net worth. There are no such filings for wealth, except after death, if ",["a large estate is left behind","https://www.armanino.com/articles/estate-valuation-tax-planning/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Wealth taxes also ",["require the annual valuation","https://rooseveltinstitute.org/wp-content/uploads/2021/03/RI_WealthTax_Report_202104.pdf"]," of businesses, farmland, artwork, intellectual property and other assets – many of which are hard to estimate."]},{"k":"p","s":["The downside of taxing income instead of wealth is that it ",["limits how much revenue can be raised","https://taxpolicycenter.org/taxvox/how-should-we-tax-rich"]," from the people most able to pay taxes. Most wealthy people convert little of their wealth into income. One common exception occurs when they ",["sell some of their stock","https://taxpolicycenter.org/taxvox/richs-real-tax-trick-isnt-buy-borrow-die"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Property taxes, like income taxes, are an exception to this rule. Calculating how much tax on real estate someone owes is easy for the authorities to do using ",["annual municipal assessments","https://www.fidelity.com/learning-center/smart-money/property-taxes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["What might happen next?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite Proposition 40’s defeat, it looks like Americans are generally open to taxing wealthy people more – at least when the states do it."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Illinois, where a billionaire governor, ",["JB Pritzer, easily won a third term","https://www.cbsnews.com/chicago/live-updates/illinois-midterm-election-results-2026-live/"],", another interesting ballot initiative prevailed."]},{"k":"p","s":["More than 75% of voters in Cook County, which includes Chicago and several of its suburbs, approved a nonbinding, advisory referendum asking if Illinois should adopt the “ ",["millionaire amendment for property tax relief and education","https://www.illinoispolicy.org/cook-county-millionaires-tax/"],".” It would levy a new surcharge of 3% on incomes over $1 million. While this win did not authorize a new tax, it revealed that support for one would be strong – at least in Chicago and Evanston."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even billionaire Bill Gates has said he believes a “ ",["billionaire’s tax","https://fortune.com/2026/11/06/bill-gates-tax-wealthy-billionaires-ai-inequality/"],"” will be necessary. The question is: What kind?"]}],"chars":7380},"https://theconversation.com/voters-rejected-data-centers-in-dozens-of-communities-fueling-the-narrative-that-opposition-to-the-ai-infrastructure-contributed-to-the-2026-blue-wave-295950":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"0ea381a1ebb73a6910ef55b502502eac51bd7423620dc8542c7838b935542e2e","read":"https://theconversation.com/voters-rejected-data-centers-in-dozens-of-communities-fueling-the-narrative-that-opposition-to-the-ai-infrastructure-contributed-to-the-2026-blue-wave-295950","bytes":187501,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Voters rejected data centers in dozens of communities, fueling the narrative that opposition to the AI infrastructure contributed to the 2026 blue wave","by":[{"n":"Barbara A. Trish","r":"Professor of Political Science, Grinnell College"}],"pub":"2026-11-09T13:43:02Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Data centers were on the ballot, both directly and indirectly, in the 2026 midterm elections."]},{"k":"p","s":["A total of ",["41 local ballot initiatives concerning data centers","https://ballotpedia.org/Data_center-related_ballot_measures,_2026"]," in 10 states were up for a vote. All but one resulted in ",["measures to restrict or limit","https://www.wsj.com/tech/ai/the-election-day-revolt-that-threatens-americas-ai-boom-03a53b52"]," their development."]},{"k":"p","s":["The centers also may have played a role in several high-profile contests. In Ohio’s ",["race for a U.S. Senate seat","https://www.wosu.org/2026-08-17/ohios-u-s-senate-candidates-recalibrate-their-stances-on-data-centers"],", Democratic challenger Sherrod Brown hammered incumbent Jon Husted for his past support of data centers. ",["In Texas, Gina Hinojosa","https://abcnews.com/Politics/texas-democrats-data-centers-winning-issue/story?id=137684995"]," made Republican Gov. Greg Abbott’s track record of supporting tax breaks for data centers a focal point of her winning campaign. Her victory marked a historic break with decades of Republican control in the state. As governor-elect, she immediately ",["reaffirmed her campaign pledge","https://www.reuters.com/world/us/texas-governor-elect-says-state-will-have-laws-shield-citizens-data-centers-2026-11-06"]," to pursue legislation protecting Texans from data centers."]},{"k":"p","s":["According to ",["NBC exit poll data","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-elections/exit-polls"],", 56% of voters felt that data centers were a major or even a crucial factor in influencing their congressional vote. For Black voters, the share was even higher, at 68%."]},{"k":"p","s":["Data centers are ",["key components in artificial intelligence infrastructure","https://www.congress.gov/crs-product/IF12899"],", housing the computing resources used to train AI models. These ",["massive facilities","https://www.nytimes.com/interactive/2026/10/05/upshot/data-center-scale.html"]," guzzle energy and water and are very noisy. Many Americans argue that their costs, in terms of ",["land use","https://www.cnbc.com/2026/09/06/ai-data-centers-are-transforming-rural-land-markets-fueling-backlash.html?msockid=3ef240ac8bed6dd42f96579a8a5d6c9d"],", higher ",["utility bills","https://www.msn.com/en-us/news/other/americans-say-rising-utility-costs-are-straining-their-budgets-they-re-blaming-data-centers/ar-AA2fTqVb?ocid=BingNewsVerp"]," and ",["environmental degradation","https://www.texastribune.org/2026/10/20/data-centers-texas-air-quality-report-pollution-health-risks/"],", outweigh the benefits."]},{"k":"p","s":["I’m a ",["professor of political science","https://www.grinnell.edu/user/trish"]," who studies political parties, electoral politics and technology. My forthcoming book, “Democratic Intelligence: Navigating Electoral Politics in an AI World,” examines how the adoption of this technology is reshaping established practices and power dynamics in campaigns."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before the midterms, it had already appeared to be disrupting some partisan alignments. Following those historic elections, which have thoroughly shaken up America’s political geography, the widespread pushback against data centers is now part of the narrative explaining the dramatic results of the 2026 midterms."]},{"k":"h","s":["Disrupting political polarization"]},{"k":"p","s":["In contrast to ",["many other issues","https://www.pewresearch.org/science/2026/05/28/americans-are-increasingly-pessimistic-about-avoiding-the-worst-effects-of-climate-change/"],", concern about data centers is relatively bipartisan. The Annenberg Public Policy Center asked Americans in mid-2026 whether they ",["support or oppose having data centers","https://www.annenbergpublicpolicycenter.org/wp-content/uploads/AI_W38_Topline.pdf"]," in their communities. Opposition was stronger among Democrats, at 69%, than Republicans, at 54%, but it crossed party lines."]},{"k":"p","s":["Local ballot measures restricting data centers also cut across traditional political alignments. Communities as disparate as deeply red Edgewater, Florida, and solidly blue Alhambra, California, voted to prohibit them. The margins for the restrictions were large, averaging 49 percentage points."]},{"k":"p","s":["The one restrictive local measure that failed to pass was in ",["Harwood, North Dakota","https://www.business-standard.com/amp/world-news/us-midterms-only-one-town-out-of-dozens-voted-in-favor-of-data-centres-126110500119_1.html"],", population around 800. With a data center project already in progress, political and economic leaders prevailed in arguing that restrictions would cut into local revenue and stifle economic development more generally."]},{"k":"h","s":["Allies and adversaries"]},{"k":"p","s":["Exit polls taken during the midterm elections also detected a degree of bipartisanship. Of the 56% of voters who said data centers ",["played a “major” or “crucial” role in their vote","https://www.nbcnews.com/politics/2026-elections/exit-polls"],", approximately two-thirds were Democrats and one-third Republicans. Exit polls, however, should be ",["interpreted with care","https://ballotpedia.org/Exit_polling"],", given their methodological limitations."]},{"k":"p","s":["These responses hint at why the ",["narrative","https://www.wired.com/story/the-results-are-in-voters-hate-data-centers/?_sp=c73d4ceb-72c9-4592-93e3-3f88045871f3.1793948422531.9d7e2aab-fdd0-4fd4-be05-bd938fd0a1a8"]," that opposition to data centers helped fuel the Democrats’ historic midterm victory emerged right away."]},{"k":"p","s":["The seeds of this argument were in place before the election, picking up on unusual alliances that marked the data center opposition. In cities and counties, zoning fights are ",["drawing a diverse kind of resistance","https://www.ap.org/news-highlights/elections/2026/in-a-divided-america-the-left-and-right-unite-to-oppose-artificial-intelligence-data-centers/"],": environmentalists, voters reeling under high electricity costs, local-control advocates and farmers concerned that data centers eat up land. They unite in opposition to projects backed by powerful corporate interests."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some of the bipartisanship around this issue has even seeped into Congress. Several weeks before Election Day, the House passed the ",["Ratepayer Protection Act","https://www.politico.com/news/2026/09/16/house-passes-bill-data-center-power-costs-01076743"]," by a 417-3 vote. The bill would require states to consider adopting a policy that data centers pay for the upgrades necessary to meet their high electricity needs. The three nay House votes were from progressives who felt the bill’s measures, which would be voluntary, didn’t go far enough to protect consumers."]},{"k":"p","s":["Similar concerns ",["killed the Senate version","https://thehill.com/policy/energy-environment/6119834-senate-data-center-bill-ratepayer-protection-act/"],", a reminder that even allies sometimes follow different strategic paths. Some proponents of tighter regulation will accept incremental progress, while others push for more sweeping change."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Brookings Institution scholars","https://www.brookings.edu/articles/how-the-2026-midterms-could-reshape-data-center-policy/"]," anticipate that the newly elected Congress will take up the issue again, this time with a directive to states to establish mandatory, not voluntary, requirements."]},{"k":"h","s":["Politics as usual"]},{"k":"p","s":["As the midterm elections approached, candidates up and down the ballot ",["blanketed the airwaves","https://adimpact.com/blogs/2026-ad-messaging-snapshot-the-quiet-boom-in-data-center-ads"]," and digital platforms with ",["ads against data centers","https://campaignsandelections.com/industry-news/ai-data-centers-emerge-as-a-hot-topic-for-political-ads-in-2026/"],". ",["President Donald Trump","https://truthsocial.com/@realDonaldTrump/posts/117190477440173795"]," pushed back, suggesting that data center opponents want their communities to be “backwards and poor.”"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Some Republican candidates","https://apnews.com/article/ai-data-centers-trump-election-cd2cfd73e3d41e2baf65bf82702a589b"]," walked a fine line between responding to voters’ concerns and not alienating the president."]},{"k":"p","s":["It matters little whether the data center electoral narrative is accurate, and so far, the reported evidence is limited. We need to know where losing candidates stood on data centers, not just the winners. That voters considered data centers important says nothing about which direction they leaned. And despite a 98% success rate across the 41 local ballot measures, it’s hard to gauge how much resistance there is to the more than ",["600 proposed data centers","https://datacenterwatch.ai/"]," that are slated to be built."]},{"k":"p","s":["What does matter is that many people apparently are accepting the narrative because that alone will affect politics and the economy. Consider ",["Elon Musk’s post on Nov. 4 on X, his social media platform","https://x.com/elonmusk/status/2117862462976594112"],": “Data centers in space looking pretty appealing right now,” and the ",["sell-off of data center-related stocks","https://apnews.com/article/stocks-markets-ai-midterm-oil-trump-7ee9c212805aa5e70cf34d25aab7a36e"]," the next day."]},{"k":"p","s":["As the 2028 presidential primaries come into focus, I believe we should expect to see many Democratic and Republican hopefuls emphasizing their support for data center restrictions and bans as they throw their hats into the ring."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some parts of this article appeared in a previous article ",["published on Oct. 26, 2026","https://theconversation.com/data-centers-are-inspiring-bipartisanship-for-now-293069"]]}],"chars":6313},"https://theconversation.com/allegheny-county-has-more-license-plate-readers-than-any-other-pa-county-heres-whats-at-stake-295948":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"e57a68db7a824df0104f803cd8ccd8c54b1735e1d5bc7c8ce5098c29446abc1b","read":"https://theconversation.com/allegheny-county-has-more-license-plate-readers-than-any-other-pa-county-heres-whats-at-stake-295948","bytes":193675,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Allegheny County has more license plate readers than any other Pa. county. Here’s what’s at stake","by":[{"n":"TK Vinod Kumar","r":"Faculty in the Law, Criminal Justice and Society Program., University of Pittsburgh"}],"pub":"2026-11-13T13:37:19Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Surveillance is a reality in the modern world. Security cameras record streets, stores, home entrances and even highways – and our phones keep track of where we go. Most of us likely don’t want to live like the characters in George Orwell’s novel “1984,” where an all-seeing government, Big Brother, is always watching. Yet technology used to fight crime has greatly increased the level of surveillance around the world."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the United States, one technology in particular has become a focus of that debate: automated license plate readers."]},{"k":"p","s":["These cameras, often mounted on poles at intersections and highway ramps, photograph every passing car. They record its plate, make, color and location, then store that information in searchable databases that police can check against lists of wanted vehicles. Flock Safety, one of the largest vendors, has cameras in ",["thousands of U.S. communities","https://theconversation.com/cameras-have-quietly-appeared-in-thousands-of-us-cities-now-their-integration-with-ai-is-sounding-alarms-276928"],", and their spread has prompted growing concern about privacy."]},{"k":"p","s":["Allegheny County in southwestern Pennsylvania, home to Pittsburgh, has ",["827 automated license plate readers","https://www.axios.com/local/pittsburgh/2026/09/14/flock-cameras-license-plate-readers-privacy-allegheny-county"],", more than any other county in the state."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Critics warn","https://www.spotlightpa.org/news/2026/09/pennsylvania-flock-camera-legislation-ban-regulations-shapiro-capitol/"]," that the cameras can map people’s daily lives with little oversight, while police say they help find stolen cars and missing people. In the borough of Munhall, just outside of Pittsburgh, ",["residents petitioned","https://www.change.org/p/demand-the-removal-of-flock-safety-surveillance-cameras-from-munhall-pa"]," to remove two Flock cameras on Main Street."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pennsylvania lawmakers from both parties have proposed at least nine bills, ranging from an outright ban of these devices to warrant requirements. In October the state House passed ",["a bill","https://www.mychesco.com/a/news/government/pennsylvania-house-passes-limits-on-license-plate-surveillance/"]," that would limit their use and how long data is kept."]},{"k":"p","s":["I study ",["policing and public order","https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=Qcp4OuoAAAAJ&hl=en"]," in democracies, and I spent more than 30 years in police administration in India and with United Nations missions abroad. I’ve seen firsthand how new technologies can help police and why they need guardrails."]},{"k":"h","s":["A spectrum of uses"]},{"k":"p","s":["How extensively police use surveillance technologies can fall anywhere across a spectrum. At one end, cameras can be positioned to monitor virtually every vehicle and person within a specified area. At the other, they are deployed sparingly and aimed only at specific vehicles or people, such as stolen cars or past offenders."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mass surveillance may entail systemic collection of data of large numbers of people in the public space, including those not suspected of any violations. These can include networks of ",["license plate readers","https://www.dhs.gov/science-and-technology/saver/automatic-license-plate-readers"]," that capture all vehicle traveling through an area, or cameras ",["using facial recognition","https://theconversation.com/how-ai-powered-policing-is-endangering-the-publics-trust-in-police-289467"]," to analyze images of individuals in public spaces against existing databases."]},{"k":"p","s":["Targeted uses include ",["matching the vehicle numbers","https://brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/automatic-license-plate-readers-legal-status-and-policy-recommendations"]," or ",["faces of people of interest","https://www.govtech.com/public-safety/pennsylvania-facial-recognition-systems-integrate-to-widen-search-for-criminals.html"],". These could be past offenders or people whose behavior raises suspicion, such as someone lingering near a bank late at night. Another example is designating certain places, such as airports, military bases, courthouses or power plants, as high-security areas and ",["deploying surveillance technology","https://www.publicsource.org/allegheny-county-sheriff-considered-facial-recognition-tech/"]," there, with or without informing the public."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the middle could be the sweet spot: calibrated use of such technology at an optimum level agreed on through laws or regulations. The level could be measured by the number of cameras in a city, the density of devices per square mile or even the terabytes of data collected."]},{"k":"h","s":["Risks of mass surveillance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Mass surveillance carries the inherent risk of the state collecting extensive information on its entire population, or on large segments of it, which creates significant potential for misuse. The state could guarantee that the data would be handled responsibly. Even so, the ",["data could be misused","https://theconversation.com/wa-police-are-scanning-faces-in-public-and-the-law-is-not-ready-for-the-consequences-286021"]," on purpose, or accessed by unauthorized persons because of vulnerabilities in data security."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also the fear of “ ",["surveillance creep","https://doi.org/10.2196/30871"],".” That is when technologies adopted for one purpose expand into others. License plate readers, for example, are typically sold to communities as a way to find stolen cars, missing children and suspects in serious crimes. But police have also used them to ",["monitor protests","https://www.eff.org/deeplinks/2025/11/how-cops-are-using-flock-safetys-alpr-network-surveil-protesters-and-activists"],". According to records obtained by nonprofit advocacy group the Electronic Frontier Foundation, agencies across the country searched Flock’s network hundreds of times in connection with protests over a single year."]},{"k":"h","s":["Potential benefits"]},{"k":"p","s":["The potential benefits of surveillance for crime prevention ",["appear to be significant","https://www.crimrxiv.com/pub/zleg04q3"],". A 2026 study of 216 law enforcement agencies found that after they installed fixed plate-reader networks, car thefts fell relative to other property crimes, and more theft cases were solved by arrest. In Atlantic City, New Jersey, a ",["major expansion of plate readers","https://www.researchwithrowan.com/en/publications/an-evaluation-of-a-major-expansion-in-automated-license-plate-rea/"]," didn’t reduce violent crime overall, but it was associated with fewer shootings, car thefts and property crimes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Other law enforcement areas that could benefit from the technology include ",["drug running","https://www.dea.gov/sites/default/files/2025-01/DEA%20NLPRP%20DEASIL%20PIA%20Revision%20-%20Final%2020241220.pdf"]," and ",["human trafficking","https://foxbaltimore.com/news/local/license-plate-readers-help-troopers-identify-maryland-man-accused-of-raping-girl-pennsylvania-motel-flock-camera-franklin-county-human-trafficking-crime-pennsylvania-pa"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Pittsburgh, ",["plate-reader data","https://www.publicsource.org/pittsburgh-flock-cameras-license-plate-readers/"]," feeds into the police bureau’s real-time crime center. The data collected could be ",["matched in real time","https://brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/automatic-license-plate-readers-legal-status-and-policy-recommendations"]," with law enforcement and other databases to track the movement of offenders."]},{"k":"p","s":["That could be used to prevent a wide range of crimes, from ",["thefts and robberies","https://www.researchwithrowan.com/en/publications/an-evaluation-of-a-major-expansion-in-automated-license-plate-rea/"]," to ",["drug running","https://www.dea.gov/sites/default/files/2025-01/DEA%20NLPRP%20DEASIL%20PIA%20Revision%20-%20Final%2020241220.pdf"]," and ",["human trafficking","https://foxbaltimore.com/news/local/license-plate-readers-help-troopers-identify-maryland-man-accused-of-raping-girl-pennsylvania-motel-flock-camera-franklin-county-human-trafficking-crime-pennsylvania-pa"],", or to help ",["solve cold cases","https://nij.ojp.gov/topics/articles/applying-modern-investigation-methods-solve-cold-cases"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["A limited approach"]},{"k":"p","s":["Limited use of such technology has the benefit of curbing misuse while still using it in a controlled manner against known offenders and threats. That means using it on a person-to-person basis with ",["prior legal or judicial approval","https://techpolicy.press/status-of-state-laws-on-facial-recognition-surveillance-continued-progress-and-smart-innovations"]," or in high-security areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["In this context, it would be most appropriate to take three steps to address law enforcement data collection generally:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Keep requiring police to get ",["court warrants backed by probable cause","https://www.aclu.org/united-states-v-carpenter-supreme-court-decision"]," for cellphone location data – records showing which cell towers a phone has connected to. That includes closing the ",["loophole","https://www.eff.org/node/104985"]," that lets agencies buy the same data from commercial brokers without a warrant."]},{"k":"li","s":["Put in place federal or state laws ",["restricting the use of facial recognition","https://www.securityindustry.org/2024/10/07/nations-strongest-regulations-for-law-enforcement-use-of-facial-recognition-technology-go-into-effect-key-provisions-of-marylands-new-law/"],", with suitable judicial oversight."]},{"k":"li","s":["Have county and municipal agencies ",["regulate the use of surveillance cameras","https://www.wesa.fm/post/council-preliminarily-approves-facial-recognition-regulation-bill"]," in public areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pennsylvania’s proposals span this range and beyond. State Sen. Dan Laughlin, an Erie Republican, would ",["ban the cameras outright","https://www.senatorlaughlin.com/2026/08/27/laughlin-plans-legislation-to-prohibit-networked-license-plate-surveillance-cameras/"],". U.S. Rep. Pat Harrigan proposes legislation ",["requiring police to get a warrant","https://harrigan.house.gov/media/press-releases/congressman-pat-harrigan-introduces-legislation-protect-americans-government"]," before searching plate-reader data. And the bill the state House passed in October sits in the middle, allowing the cameras but ",["limiting their uses","https://www.billtrack50.com/billdetail/2013588"]," and how long data is kept."]},{"k":"h","s":["Guardrails"]},{"k":"p","s":["Decisions regarding the use of mass cameras should not be left to law enforcement agencies. They are interested in crime control, which could color their judgment. Those decisions are ",["best left to elected representatives","https://www.publicsource.org/pittsburgh-city-council-vote-regulate-facial-recognition/"]," at the federal, state and local levels, with input from legal experts and relevant law enforcement agencies."]},{"k":"p","s":["In my view, mandatory ",["public consultation","https://www.aclum.org/campaigns-initiatives/community-control-over-police-surveillance-ccops/"]," before deploying such systems in a community would improve the legitimacy of the program and of the implementing government. Regular audits are a common safeguard when government agencies use intrusive technology. Pennsylvania’s House-passed plate-reader bill, for instance, ",["would require agencies","https://www.mychesco.com/a/news/government/pennsylvania-house-passes-limits-on-license-plate-surveillance/"]," to adopt audit policies. Such audits could happen as often as twice a year, with information and analyses available to the community or to affected individuals on request."]},{"k":"p","s":["Transparency of the process would go a long way toward enhancing public trust. The opposite can erode it. At Penn State, for example, the university ",["initially declined to say","https://www.govtech.com/education/higher-ed/penn-state-pulls-flock-cameras-over-cost-but-might-use-other-cameras"]," how many plate-reader cameras it had installed or where, drawing criticism from students before it ended its contract with Flock."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another precaution is to keep the data from being available in raw form to nongovernmental entities, especially corporations. Location records can be valuable to businesses. Companies already ",["use plate-reader data","https://brennancenter.org/our-work/research-reports/automatic-license-plate-readers-legal-status-and-policy-recommendations"]," for purposes such as verifying a loan applicant’s home address."]},{"k":"p","s":["As Pennsylvania lawmakers weigh new limits, the choices they make may help determine how close any of us come to living in an Orwellian state."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more of our stories about ",["Pittsburgh and Pennsylvania","https://theconversation.com/us/pittsburgh-news"],"."]}],"chars":8041},"https://theconversation.com/us-and-iran-once-practiced-diplomacy-through-archaeology-that-legacy-need-not-lie-in-ruins-292886":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-19T14:33Z","sha":"3e79f0af033332ef3953482acbb1221e73ead13dbc5e3079bd8c747ffa946a5f","read":"https://theconversation.com/us-and-iran-once-practiced-diplomacy-through-archaeology-that-legacy-need-not-lie-in-ruins-292886","bytes":189645,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"US and Iran once practiced diplomacy through archaeology – that legacy need not lie in ruins","by":[{"n":"Kyle Olson","r":"Lecturer in Archaeology, Washington University in St. Louis"}],"pub":"2026-11-19T13:42:48Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["When a U.S. airstrike ",["struck Tehran’s Arg Square","https://www.the-independent.com/news/world/middle-east/iran-golestan-palace-damaged-airstrike-us-israel-war-b2930842.html"]," on March 2, 2026, Golestan Palace was not the target. But it was close enough."]},{"k":"p","s":["The missile’s impact blew out windows across the palace complex and damaged some of its elaborate 19th-century interiors. In ",["photographs taken afterward","https://www.businessinsider.com/golestan-palace-iran-strikes-damage-photos-2026-3"],", pieces of its celebrated mirrorwork lay scattered across the floor."]},{"k":"p","s":["Golestan is a ",["UNESCO World Heritage Site","https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/1422/"]," and one of the great surviving monuments of Iran’s Qajar dynasty, which ruled from 1789 until 1925. Within hours of the strike, ",["UNESCO reported the damage","https://www.unesco.org/en/articles/unesco-expresses-concern-over-protection-cultural-heritage-sites-amidst-escalating-violence-middle?hub=80094"]," and noted that cultural property is protected under international law during armed conflict."]},{"k":"p","s":["The palace was not only an early casualty of the U.S.-Iran war, but a symbolically potent one, too. And as my colleague Mehrnoush Soroush at the Center for Ancient Middle Eastern Landscapes ",["has documented","https://heritagewatch.camelab.net/"],", Golestan is not alone. Since the war in Iran began in February 2026, reports of ",["damage to heritage sites have poured in","https://the-european.eu/story-68260/irans-historic-treasures-face-destruction-as-war-puts-centuries-of-heritage-at-risk.html"]," from all across Iran."]},{"k":"p","s":["I know that damaged buildings — no matter how valuable — cannot compare with the human costs of war. But the images from Golestan have particular resonance to me, an archaeologist who ",["studies the history of relations between Iran and the United States","https://anthropology.washu.edu/people/kyle-g-olson"],". It also cuts against a history of cooperation between American and Iranian archaeologists, in which Americans worked to preserve, rather than destroy, Iranian heritage."]},{"k":"h","s":["Digging in, together"]},{"k":"p","s":["I have spent years researching how archaeologists, museums and cultural officials from the two countries worked together before the ",["Iranian Revolution of 1979","https://www.brookings.edu/articles/the-iranian-revolution-a-timeline-of-events/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["My ",["earlier research has examined","https://doi.org/10.1080/02757206.2023.2261972"]," how archaeology became entangled with American foreign aid and Iranian development programs during the 1960s, and I am currently writing a book on the history of U.S.-Iranian heritage diplomacy over the past century."]},{"k":"p","s":["I believe that history offers another way of thinking about what has been lost in the current conflict. Long before Iran and the U.S. became adversaries, cultural heritage provided a setting in which people from the two countries learned how to work together."]},{"k":"p","s":["American archaeologists ",["began excavating in Iran in the early 1930s","https://www.bloomsbury.com/uk/americaniranian-dialogues-9781350118720/"],". In those days, the relationship was unequal: American museums sought access to archaeological sites and, under agreements with the Iranian government, received portions of the objects they excavated under the ",["colonial system of partage","https://smarthistory.org/partage/"],". As a result, ",["museums","https://collections.penn.museum/collections/search.php?term=iran&submit_term=Submit"]," across the U.S. still hold substantial collections of Iranian antiquities."]},{"k":"p","s":["The terms of the relationship changed considerably during the 1960s, as the U.S. and Iran intensified their connections. At the same time that thousands of American professionals, educators, businesspeople, scholars and others came to work and live in Iran, the country ",["revised its antiquities laws and expanded its own archaeological institutions, universities and museums","https://doi.org/10.1080/1743873X.2022.2096457"],", resulting in, among other things, ",["a major tourism boom","https://ajammc.com/2023/07/14/destination-persia-tourism-1960s/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["American archaeologists still wanted permission to dig at Iranian sites, but they increasingly operated within a system controlled by Iranian officials. In return, American institutions contributed funding and access to laboratories, specialist knowledge, graduate education and connections to an international scholarly community."]},{"k":"p","s":["American archaeological projects in Iran drew on large networks of such connections. Scholars ",["working on the Deh Luran Plain","https://muse.jhu.edu/book/81281"]," in southwestern Iran, for example, depended on Iranian government agencies, the U.S. Embassy, American universities and museums, development organizations and scientific laboratories. Botanical remains, animal bones and other materials moved through specialist laboratories abroad, while Iranian officials worked alongside foreign researchers in the field."]},{"k":"h","s":["Collaboration under the shah"]},{"k":"p","s":["By the 1970s, ",["fieldwork projects","https://doi.org/10.4324/9781003224129"]," were increasingly becoming joint enterprises, based on formal partnerships between institutions and cooperative leadership. Iranian archaeological authorities employed American specialists to help ",["survey areas threatened by dams and other development projects","https://press.umich.edu/Books/A/Archaeological-Investigations-in-Northeastern-Xuzestan-1976"],", while Iranian archaeologists increasingly took leading roles in the field. Meanwhile, students moved in greater numbers between Tehran, Chicago, Philadelphia and New York. Museums organized ",["traveling exhibitions","https://www.artforum.com/features/iranian-art-211785/"],", and Iran hosted ",["international scholarly congresses","https://search.worldcat.org/title/469523400"]," devoted to its history and archaeology."]},{"k":"p","s":["It can’t be ignored that these collaborations flourished during a period when Iran, under Mohammad Reza Shah Pahlavi, ",["was a close American ally","https://www.pbs.org/wgbh/americanexperience/features/taken-hostage-presidents-shah-strategic-partnership/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["While the terms of the relationship increasingly favored Iran, they were still marked by geopolitical inequalities. American universities and museums possessed resources that Iranian institutions often lacked – not only financially and in terms of human capital, but physically, in the form of collections of artifacts that had previously been taken out of Iran."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet the collaborations also developed lives of their own, as American scholars returned year after year."]},{"k":"h","s":["Post-revolutionary changes"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Islamic Revolution","https://www.brookings.edu/articles/the-iranian-revolution-a-timeline-of-events/"]," exposed both how extensive and fragile this network was. Even as the crisis that began in 1978 deepened, American archaeologists did not initially assume that their Iranian partnerships were finished. At Malyan, the remains of ancient Anshan, ",["archaeologist William Sumner","https://commons.library.stonybrook.edu/amar/157/"]," proposed continuing to pay a watchman to protect the site, while maintaining contact with Iranian colleagues so research could eventually resume."]},{"k":"p","s":["That did not come to pass. And much of the American-Iranian archaeological enterprise collapsed as diplomatic relations between the two countries soured after the Islamic Republic took 52 American diplomats and civilians ",["hostage in 1979","https://history.state.gov/departmenthistory/short-history/iraniancrises"]," and Washington sided with Baghdad during the ",["Iran-Iraq War","https://www.britannica.com/event/Iran-Iraq-War"]," in the 1980s."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the example of the 1960s and ‘70s points toward a sometimes less visible part of diplomacy: relationships accumulated through repeated practical work."]},{"k":"p","s":["International relations expert Trita Parsi makes this point in his history of the negotiations that produced the ",["2015 Iran nuclear agreement","https://www.cfr.org/backgrounders/what-iran-nuclear-deal"],". In “ ",["Losing an Enemy","https://yalebooks.yale.edu/book/9780300218169/losing-an-enemy/"],",” based on interviews with participants on both sides, Parsi describes the working relationship that developed between U.S. Secretary of State John Kerry and Iranian Foreign Minister Mohammad Javad Zarif."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is not to say that their personal rapport produced the nuclear agreement by itself. Naturally, presidents had to authorize negotiations, diplomats at all levels had to find compromises, and both governments had to conclude that an agreement served their interests. But ",["contemporary reporting","https://www.washingtonpost.com/world/national-security/how-john-and-javad-learned-to-work-together-on-an-iran-deal/2015/07/03/c1dd3ffa-cb17-40c3-ac37-a97c4f495b65_story.html"]," described that relationship as one built on professional respect and repeated close proximity. In other words, Kerry and Zarif spent enough time negotiating together to understand each other’s constraints and establish a working relationship despite the hostility between their two governments."]},{"k":"p","s":["That kind of personal working relationship can assist diplomacy – not just at the highest levels but more broadly across civil society. ",["Sports diplomacy","https://www.state.gov/sports-diplomacy"]," has long been acknowledged; so too the ",["sharing of zoological “gifts.”","https://www.history.com/articles/panda-diplomacy-the-worlds-cutest-ambassadors"]," My research shows that archaeology has long had an important a place in these kinds of cultural exchanges as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["Today, Iranian conservation specialists are sorting and cataloging shattered fragments from Golestan Palace while attempting to ",["repair damage at heritage sites around the country","https://www.theartnewspaper.com/2026/09/04/irans-heritage-experts-race-to-repair-damaged-sites-as-negotiations-stall"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["At the same time, American and Iranian officials are still looking for ways to end the conflict. I don’t know what U.S.-Iranian relations will look like when the fighting eventually ends, but damaged buildings and monuments will need to be repaired and conserved. If my inbox is anything to go by, Iranian scholars still want to work together with American colleagues."]},{"k":"p","s":["And if a larger political opening for U.S.-Iranian rapprochement ever arrives, the relationships built by those who steward and study Iran’s heritage may matter more than they first appear."]}],"chars":7929}};
